{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek","id":1460589,"title":"Sabbat Book take a peek!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-20T15:58:17-07:00","id":1460589,"title":"Sabbat Book take a peek!","content":"Permission has been given to an influencer to take a peek at the pages of the Sabbat book. Looking at it in detail, we can flush down the theory of some that the book was being marketed as a book for antagonists simply to circumvent censorship and backfire. Below is a print, the full video is at the end of the post:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QDhbz7H.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;IN STORIES<br /> <br /> The most obvious call to action for a Blood Feast is to somehow<br /> stop it, and if that's not possible, peharps even to recover some number<br /> of the victims.<br /> A Blood Feast is a true test of morality, for even<br /> if the player's coterie isn't' a bunch of do-gooders,<br /> chronicle Tenets, personal Convictions and the self-preservation<br /> function of the Masquerade may urge characters to prevent<br /> innocents from meeting gruesome ends.<br /> Some victims might even be procured ofr nights before the Ritae's culmination,<br /> and those close to them might notice that they've gone missing - often to little<br /> avail. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> The print information is in line with the marketing done by the developers: this is a book for antagonists. The Ritae in this book, for example, just describes what the PCs might react to when they receive news that the ritual has happened or is about to happen (and how they are likely to try to prevent such cruelty from happening).<br /> <br /> The full video is available here: <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/foryou?_d=secCgYIASAHKAESPgo8i0CqwQTGlNrjPf9CaCxEsk99MlIQxvrANbixQrJsFFv8SARKlclVV5V%2Btcokopd6DbZOCyNvAweU9D1xGgA%3D&amp;checksum=593f59fd5f847431d90f064e08e8d1118479af0ee43cd566f7bf2c24380ffab4&amp;language=en&amp;preview_pb=0&amp;sec_user_id=MS4wLjABAAAAaf12tA4HPS1XNYd57Jp8uYuICd3H9pWGrya9qO4W1FHdTmrPHq29oMHWVQz0PB6r&amp;share_app_id=1233&amp;share_item_id=7010066005368081670&amp;share_link_id=9ef174ad-3182-4008-9ccd-4d17884596bc&amp;source=h5_m&amp;timestamp=1632158950&amp;u_code=d782cb0fccdh44&amp;user_id=6713602884838032390&amp;utm_campaign=client_share&amp;utm_medium=android&amp;utm_source=copy&amp;_r=1&amp;is_copy_url=1&amp;is_from_webapp=v1&amp;item_id=7010066005368081670#/@mattstormcrow/video/7010066005368081670\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tiktok.com/foryou?_d=sec...66005368081670</a></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T00:31:07-07:00","id":1460621,"title":"","content":"Path of the sun: &quot;there's a thin blood path now, awesome&quot; <br /> <br /> Sounds like false enthusiasm. Almost sarcasm. Can't they pay him more to shill harder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T04:19:32-07:00","id":1460628,"title":"","content":"The art looks a lot better than anarch or corebook even if they're still going for that faux realistic style, I approve of the lack of photoshoots-especially for the alien nightmarish sabbat. The layout looks a lot better too. Hopefully they'll be enough to reverse engineer a player game to justify the price.<br /> <br /> Incidently it's still a horrible horrible mistake to not have them playable with a $45 price tag but babysteps forward here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-21-2021, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T04:51:03-07:00","id":1460629,"title":"","content":"To be honest, even as someone who first dabbled into the WoD/CoD on a play by forum with a Sabbat City Gangrel, I can understand why OPP may have grown worried/squeamish with the Sabbat as a playable faction.<br /> <br /> It does take away from the personal horror side of the game after all. And I never really liked the sort of &quot;devil's rejet&quot; vibe that all the antitribu had for me, making them severely lacking in term of Clan representation, traditions and the like...<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs aren't exactly hyper attractive against the Camarilla. OPP would needs to flesh them out, make them distinct and perhaps built them off the Clans comprising them to make them sustainable in the long run. But they don't seem to know what to do with them sadly.<br /> <br /> I'd rather play devil's reject Gangrel than &quot;aimless Gangrel doing something I don't know&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T04:54:56-07:00","id":1460630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460629#post1460629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does take away from the personal horror side of the game after all. And I never really liked the sort of &amp;quot;devil's rejet&amp;quot; vibe that all the antitribu had for me, making them severely lacking in term of Clan representation, traditions and the like...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for a good film on how Sabbat work as a horror sect I'd recommend Near dark. It's pitch perfect and does everything devils rejects does way better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T06:27:43-07:00","id":1460646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460629#post1460629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, even as someone who first dabbled into the WoD/CoD on a play by forum with a Sabbat City Gangrel, I can understand why OPP may have grown worried/squeamish with the Sabbat as a playable faction.<br /> <br /> It does take away from the personal horror side of the game after all. And I never really liked the sort of &quot;devil's rejet&quot; vibe that all the antitribu had for me, making them severely lacking in term of Clan representation, traditions and the like...<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs aren't exactly hyper attractive against the Camarilla. OPP would needs to flesh them out, make them distinct and perhaps built them off the Clans comprising them to make them sustainable in the long run. But they don't seem to know what to do with them sadly.<br /> <br /> I'd rather play devil's reject Gangrel than &quot;aimless Gangrel doing something I don't know&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OPP didn't write this (or the Anarch book), it was written in-house by the WoD Brand Team. And Justin Achilli pretty directly laid out the reason for non-playable Sabbat when he was interviewed about it: Humanity and the struggle with it and the Beast is the 'core theme' of Vampire, and especially in 5th Edition, and the Sabbat are the antithesis to that, throwing it away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T06:36:18-07:00","id":1460649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460646#post1460646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OPP didn't write this (or the Anarch book), it was written in-house by the WoD Brand Team. And Justin Achilli pretty directly laid out the reason for non-playable Sabbat when he was interviewed about it: Humanity and the struggle with it and the Beast is the 'core theme' of Vampire, and especially in 5th Edition, and the Sabbat are the antithesis to that, throwing it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure and I agree with him that if V5 aim is a return to personnal horror and the slow erosion of one's Humanity the Sabbat is a problem with its paths allowing them to basically sidestep the whole deal and go full gore with little consequences...<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs are kind of a downgrade nonetheless because they are too messy and ill-defined. What do they want? How is it different from the Cams ? The Sabbat at least as a very clear and distinct vibe which has grown over time. <br /> <br /> There is a reason it usurped the Anarchs position as the second big playable factions, after all.<br /> <br /> Ps : I have no ideas how OPP and the inside team or whatever its named work as entities, separate or otherwise \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T07:03:55-07:00","id":1460660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460646#post1460646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OPP didn't write this (or the Anarch book), it was written in-house by the WoD Brand Team. And Justin Achilli pretty directly laid out the reason for non-playable Sabbat when he was interviewed about it: Humanity and the struggle with it and the Beast is the 'core theme' of Vampire, and especially in 5th Edition, and the Sabbat are the antithesis to that, throwing it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the classic issue which has bugged vtm for decades : the one true way to run it fallacy. Scourge of modern gaming. Imagine if ravenloft was re envisioned to just be spoopy forgotten realms....oh wait nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-21-2021, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T07:48:14-07:00","id":1460669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460660#post1460660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah the classic issue which has bugged vtm for decades : the one true way to run it fallacy. Scourge of modern gaming. Imagine if ravenloft was re envisioned to just be spoopy forgotten realms....oh wait nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it\u2019s the struggle between VtM as a specific IP useful for other media and VtM as a toolkit for vampire-themed campaigns. The one true way is what the managers have determined that promoting will be best for expanding the IP, while the player base wants the same toolkit V20 provided, just with streamlined tools (but which probably wouldn\u2019t do much to expand the IP beyond its current fans).<br /> <br /> Another way to put it is that devs want you playing the computer equivalent of the latest well-written CRPG while the players who are unhappy with the direction V5 is going wanted it to be more like Minecraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T08:07:06-07:00","id":1460673,"title":"","content":"I'm glad this book is coming out but I feel like they should have added player options for the Sabbat, damn the torpedoes.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because I am a guy who owns FREAK LEGION and CLAN BOOK: BAALI. I always felt we needed Infernalist and Nephandi rules beyond the BOOK OF MADNESS too.<br /> <br /> As big a fan of V5 as I am, I don't think we should shy away from purely evil protagonists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T08:21:11-07:00","id":1460675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460660#post1460660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah the classic issue which has bugged vtm for decades : the one true way to run it fallacy. Scourge of modern gaming. Imagine if ravenloft was re envisioned to just be spoopy forgotten realms....oh wait nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I think one of the main but underlying problems of V5, the Anarchs being underwhelming and too close to the Camarilla in practice was explained well enough in a Requiem thread by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> : the writers being from the US have a view were political factions are mostly unchanging and yet overlapse a lot. Democrats and Republicans are a lot closer as parties than similar divided political factions elsewhere in the western world. <br /> <br /> Even if it's less true today, for a very long time, as an outsider, I saw very little difference between the two but there was some form of &quot;tribalism&quot; with people strongly associating to their party even if they represented perhaps only a fraction of it. But the opposition between such forces is largely irrelevant. It doesn't matter if you vote Democrat or Republican if they agree on 75% of their programs basically.<br /> <br /> That's the Anarchs and Camarilla in a nutshell. The Anarchs don't seem to want to fundamentaly change Vampiric society. They want to tweak it, make it fairer for young Vamps, sure... but they do'nt fundamentaly oppose its tenets and rules. The Sabbat does and that's definitively what attracted me to them back in the day. If I wanted to play the ones saying &quot;Fuck your system, I hate it, and I'll take you down with it...&quot; well, it's Sabbat or bust basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T08:29:56-07:00","id":1460677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460628#post1460628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art looks a lot better than anarch or corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be really hard to be worse. This lesson at least they learned, and that is to say something.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460629#post1460629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does take away from the personal horror side of the game after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> said, this is a fallacy.<br /> <br /> No matter what theme you intend for the game, in the end every setting is bound to be used in different ways by the players and working with it instead of against it is a better general design strategy. I do think the Sabbat isn't the best developed idea they had in VtM, but ditching it isn't nearly a solution to anything. What, they think they're my mom to say which theme I have to play? The game is big, and growing again. Keeping to a single theme is putting unnecessary constraints on development and basically shooting yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460669#post1460669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it\u2019s the struggle between VtM as a specific IP useful for other media and VtM as a toolkit for vampire-themed campaigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such struggle and the players hardly want a Minecraft. WoD has never been the most open ended toolkit to begin with, it is one of the most strictly constrained settings in the market, with the metaplot stating the state of almost everything, their relationships, the options you have and so on. CoD is infinitely more like a toolkit than V20 and I'm still hard pressed to say it is like Minecraft.<br /> <br /> But they sure are doing this out of a desire of exploring other media. This is all too obvious, esp. with the corebook illustration, it was a strong telltale. It just isn't a struggle and isn't a smart way to do this, either. There is no need for the RPG book to look like the videogame will. There is no need for the RPG book to use the same plots and themes they <b>think</b> the games will use. Their focus is to make games, sure, and I sincerely think it's perfectly fine. But making the RPG like that isn't really going to help.<br /> <br /> And this isn't just me saying. They are basically doing a dumber variation of WotC strategy with D&amp;D 4th, the difference being that in D&amp;D their focus was to attract MMO players to the RPG instead of taking RPG players to the MMO, and it worked, no matter how much the D&amp;D community complained. But it wasn't a good long term strategy and 4th edition was the shortest lived since the early 80s. 5th edition refocused into making the game more open and well built and actually attracted more developers and players to other media than 4th was capable of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460675#post1460675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the writers being from the US have a view were political factions are mostly unchanging and yet overlapse a lot. Democrats and Republicans are a lot closer as parties than similar divided political factions elsewhere in the western world.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of that. Americans are too used to the idea that the actual ideological fight is in the primaries and that everyone belongs to a party. But that arrangement actually only exists in the US. Outside we're very used to see radically distinct parties disputing elections, there's no &quot;everyone is a member of a party&quot; either. So the Cam and Anarchs pretty much started as the Republicans vs Democrats and the Sabbat apparently came to be the Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T08:45:19-07:00","id":1460681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460677#post1460677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> said, this is a fallacy.<br /> <br /> No matter what theme you intend for the game, in the end every setting is bound to be used in different ways by the players and working with it instead of against it is a better general design strategy. I do think the Sabbat isn't the best developed idea they had in VtM, but ditching it isn't nearly a solution to anything. What, they think they're my mom to say which theme I have to play? The game is big, and growing again. Keeping to a single theme is putting unnecessary constraints on development and basically shooting yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree wholeheartedly. I just understand why they'd think the Sabbat would undermine what they consider to be the core of the game. However, let's be honest, there is nothing inherent to the Paths preventing it from still happening. Instead of them being entirely separated from Humanity it should have been possible to tweak them to make them mitigator or something like that without destroying the identity of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T09:00:01-07:00","id":1460683,"title":"","content":"I'm not surprised by Ritae was written this way; its an antagonist book. They had already lost me with that and saying basically the style of vtm I want to play isn't welcome anymore which made me sad. I did run some number which are amusing.<br /> <br /> In 1999 when the Guide to the Sabbat was released it was 224 pages for 42.61 (adjusted for inflation, originally went for 25.95), this book is 140 pages for for 45 dollars. Besides the fact I can't really use it for running a Sabbat game besides..ehh make up the rest. The value is simply not the same for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T09:04:00-07:00","id":1460684,"title":"","content":"It's a mistake to insist that that be the core of the game to begin with. Different people want different things from the game. Insisting that there is only One True Way is a mistake. It's like selling hamburgers and insisting that everyone eats it with pickles. Not everyone likes their hamburgers with friggin pickles. Some people might want you to hold the pickles and add extra mustard. Getting preachy about how every last customer should and must eat the pickles and you're scum if you don't eat the damned pickles is a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T09:32:38-07:00","id":1460687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460649#post1460649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure and I agree with him that if V5 aim is a return to personnal horror and the slow erosion of one's Humanity the Sabbat is a problem with its paths allowing them to basically sidestep the whole deal and go full gore with little consequences...<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs are kind of a downgrade nonetheless because they are too messy and ill-defined. What do they want? How is it different from the Cams ? The Sabbat at least as a very clear and distinct vibe which has grown over time.<br /> <br /> There is a reason it usurped the Anarchs position as the second big playable factions, after all.<br /> <br /> Ps : I have no ideas how OPP and the inside team or whatever its named work as entities, separate or otherwise \ud83d\ude05</div> </div> </div> </div>At least on the Anarchs, that's largely their point. You're given their baselines in the book, and, unlike prior editions (or a bunch of media like Bloodlines), things like Baronies and setups with the Anarchs as 'Cam Lite' aren't what they are anymore. The Anarchs are a movement, not a hegemony, and also not organized in any way, so you have a huge diaspora of 'what it means to be an anarch'. The Anarch book for V5 illustrates this in its variety of articles and such.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, re: core themes. Beyond the stated core themes of Vampire, and V5 specifically, a lot of people (especially people in this thread) also forget that this stuff isn't being written Just For Existing Players. They've stated before, both directly and indirectly, that the tabletop game exists to provide 'backbone' for story and such for their other media products. Anything being written for the TTRPG is also being looked at for how it'll look as 1. stuff to adapt/transition to things like TV and video games, and 2. how it'll look to people coming into the property through those things. And so going with a defined theme and tone and setup, including a defined antagonist group, makes that infinitely easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 09-21-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T09:57:40-07:00","id":1460689,"title":"","content":"Eh, Don't play that card. V5 has made factions more obtuse and difficult to understand, with far more subfactions (church of Caine, four kinds of Tremere, Ministry AND church of Set) and has greatly muddled the lexicon with stuff like Mawla/Chasse. Nothing about V5 is more newb or TV friendly. Rather the opposite actually; Cementing who these factions are undermines the flexiblity of writers. Before we could have chosen to depict the Cam as a model society, as a hellhole, a neccessary evil, the shield of kine, competent or incompetent. Now they're only an elite caricature from the perspective of a white american liberal or whatever. Writers need options, not a silly predetermined jigsaw puzzle with too many pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T10:48:45-07:00","id":1460692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460689#post1460689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Don't play that card. V5 has made factions more obtuse and difficult to understand, with far more subfactions (church of Caine, four kinds of Tremere, Ministry AND church of Set) and has greatly muddled the lexicon with stuff like Mawla/Chasse. Nothing about V5 is more newb or TV friendly. Rather the opposite actually; Cementing who these factions are undermines the flexiblity of writers. <b>Before we could have chosen to depict the Cam as a model society, as a hellhole, a neccessary evil, the shield of kine, competent or incompetent. Now they're only an elite caricature from the perspective of a white american liberal or whatever. Writers need options, not a silly predetermined jigsaw puzzle with too many pieces.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to point out the obvious but Revised stated overtly the Camarilla was every bit as evil and vile as the Sabbat as of 1998. The whole &quot;Scourge&quot; thing was to illustrate they were an awful group of tyrants and, furthermore, their cities were described as poverty stricken crime-ridden hellholes.<br /> <br /> This is not a product of V5.<br /> <br /> It's literally 22 years old and most of the game's history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T10:50:04-07:00","id":1460693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460687#post1460687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least on the Anarchs, that's largely their point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> To begin with, this isn't anything new. It is what the Anarchs were since day 1 of the game, all the way back to 1991. Not a block, but the multitude of people that didn't belong in the system, either by slipping through the cracks and not trying to go back, or by actively antagonizing it. Baronies are just a title never meant to mean much beyond 'the big boss in town isn't Cam'.<br /> <br /> And the problem is precisely that the Anarchs rarely got defined beyond that. They also were meant to be the protagonists since day 1, you live under Camarilla's control but you're not a part of it. The problem? As such, the Anarchs went undefined. The Camarilla was fleshed out, the Sabbat was fleshed out, and the Anarchs stayed a bunch of 'something'. The players went to play other things and the Anarchs laid more or less on the sideways. A lot of tables and LARPs ignored the Anarchs royally.<br /> <br /> It isn't by mere coincidence that players renewed interest in the Anarchs with V20. Giving actual flesh to the Movement was something badly needed. You don't need to make them a hegemony to do this, either, just create their context. Sample <b>movements and political struggles</b>, instead of an endless parade of sample boring kids with no idea of what they'll do with politics. And at the same time, not being a hegemony, somehow seizing power more than ever because the Camarilla suddenly can't stop the Anarchs if they get dumber.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460687#post1460687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the stated core themes of Vampire, and V5 specifically, a lot of people (especially people in this thread) also forget that this stuff isn't being written Just For Existing Players.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only conclusion is that you're not reading some posts, because despite a lot of people complaining about their personal situation, most posts are about things that apply pretty well to new players.<br /> <br /> Yes, the lore of VtM up to V20 is overwhelming and making some simplifications, especially on the core, helps a lot to make it welcoming to newcomers, which is a big deal.<br /> <br /> What on frigging Hell does that have anything to do with the Sabbat being playable? Do they get to be less antagonistic 'cause of that? They've have always been the default antagonists of the game, they getting fans never changed that not even in (most of) their fans minds. They're receiving a treatment in their own book that they should have received in the core, because THAT's the book to make a quick presentation of antagonists as just that, instead of saying your antagonists can't attend the game 'cause they're occupied fighting in Afghanistan (and somehow despite the extensive media coverage the Middle East receives nowadays no one ever noticed an open war among eldritch horrors there).<br /> <br /> From post #5 onward a lot of posts cover either how this idea of over simplification doesn't help with movies, doesn't help with videogames, doesn't help with player experience, doesn't help streamlining the themes of the game, and aren't even something new. RPGs have existed for almost 50 years now. Vampire for 30. Multimedia franchises have been a professional strategy in this market for about 15 years consistently. They're not treading unknown waters and are making rookie mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T11:41:31-07:00","id":1460699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460675#post1460675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funnily enough, I think one of the main but underlying problems of V5, the Anarchs being underwhelming and too close to the Camarilla in practice was explained well enough in a Requiem thread by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> : the writers being from the US have a view were political factions are mostly unchanging and yet overlapse a lot. Democrats and Republicans are a lot closer as parties than similar divided political factions elsewhere in the western world.<br /> <br /> Even if it's less true today, for a very long time, as an outsider, I saw very little difference between the two but there was some form of &quot;tribalism&quot; with people strongly associating to their party even if they represented perhaps only a fraction of it. But the opposition between such forces is largely irrelevant. It doesn't matter if you vote Democrat or Republican if they agree on 75% of their programs basically.<br /> <br /> That's the Anarchs and Camarilla in a nutshell. The Anarchs don't seem to want to fundamentaly change Vampiric society. They want to tweak it, make it fairer for young Vamps, sure... but they do'nt fundamentaly oppose its tenets and rules. The Sabbat does and that's definitively what attracted me to them back in the day. If I wanted to play the ones saying &quot;Fuck your system, I hate it, and I'll take you down with it...&quot; well, it's Sabbat or bust basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's never been Republicans versus Democrats because one side is absolutely in charge (The Camarilla) and the other side is, by definition, on the backfoot (The Anarchs). They're also living in a feudal not democratic society. Mind you, I've never accepted the view that Anarchs viewed <i>themselves</i> as part of the Camarilla. The Camarilla might consider themselves as having authority over the Anarchs but the whole essential argument to me has always been the Anarchs do not recognize the authority of the Prince or his court.<br /> <br /> I've always felt that the best analog for them has been to emphasize the Gothic PUNK element and have thought the gameline was a supernatural version of Cyberpunk 2020. The Camarilla are the Corpos. They are rich, in charge, and a bunch of bastards. The Anarchs are the criminals, Edgerunners, and syndicates that live on the edge of society and out of the corpos control but with their own brutal society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T11:51:21-07:00","id":1460703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460699#post1460699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt that the best analog for them has been to emphasize the Gothic PUNK element and have thought the gameline was a supernatural version of Cyberpunk 2020.</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS kind of that, but without understanding how this works elsewhere, apparently, the devs basically made them be the Punk Movement against The Man, but have the social and political dynamics of american parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T11:52:52-07:00","id":1460704,"title":"","content":"<br /> They are terribly afraid to publish anything that might cause a negative reaction, as with the chapter on Chechnya, and that it will hinder the use of the IP in other medias.<br /> <br /> I really like the Sabbat and the themes it brings, although I've never played a chronicle focused on them, but I think it's hard not to agree that a book released today doesn't make it clear that they're just the &quot;villains&quot; and that you shouldn't play with them would attract the attention of many people, even non-players, who might criticize and point out that many of the Sabbat's themes and methods would be endorsed by the authors.<br /> <br /> I don't think what the Sabbat represents, its methods, paths, rites and actions would hinder what can be done in other media, but the mere idea of \u200b\u200bthe negative publicity that a book like this could provoke makes WW not want to risk it.<br /> <br /> This is a recurrent problem in the current times when you want to turn everything into multimedia franchises, the fear of provoking adverse feelings makes everything be done in the safest way possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","name":"Mark Logan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:19:31-07:00","id":1460712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460704#post1460704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are terribly afraid to publish anything that might cause a negative reaction, as with the chapter on Chechnya, and that it will hinder the use of the IP in other medias.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's publishers in Russia almost got arrested over that. But yes, vampire is only effective when it's for adults and contains mature content. Which is what V5 claimed it was about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:32:05-07:00","id":1460715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460704#post1460704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are terribly afraid to publish anything that might cause a negative reaction, as with the chapter on Chechnya, and that it will hinder the use of the IP in other medias.<br /> <br /> I really like the Sabbat and the themes it brings, although I've never played a chronicle focused on them, but I think it's hard not to agree that a book released today doesn't make it clear that they're just the &quot;villains&quot; and that you shouldn't play with them would attract the attention of many people, even non-players, who might criticize and point out that many of the Sabbat's themes and methods would be endorsed by the authors.<br /> <br /> I don't think what the Sabbat represents, its methods, paths, rites and actions would hinder what can be done in other media, but the mere idea of \u200b\u200bthe negative publicity that a book like this could provoke makes WW not want to risk it.<br /> <br /> This is a recurrent problem in the current times when you want to turn everything into multimedia franchises, the fear of provoking adverse feelings makes everything be done in the safest way possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were the case then vtm would be stillborn, all three of the sects are evil and full of awful awful people doing awful things. In fact they made the anarchs and cams worse than in previous editions. The chechya incident obviously being the worst offender because it broke the golden rule about irl politics but even the more....wholesome sections are pretty demented irl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-21-2021, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:47:47-07:00","id":1460717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460715#post1460715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that were the case then vtm would be stillborn, all three of the sects are evil and full of awful awful people doing awful things. <b>In fact they made the anarchs and cams worse than in previous editions. </b>The chechya incident obviously being the worst offender because it broke the golden rule about irl politics but even the more....wholesome sections are pretty demented irl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's been the case since Revised.<br /> <br /> The V5 version is not noticeably worse than the immediate previous editions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:54:32-07:00","id":1460718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460699#post1460699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I've never accepted the view that Anarchs viewed <i>themselves</i> as part of the Camarilla. The Camarilla might consider themselves as having authority over the Anarchs but the whole essential argument to me has always been the Anarchs do not recognize the authority of the Prince or his court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I've never accepted the view that the Princes and the Camarilla are synonymous. <b><i>The office of the Prince is older than the Camarilla.</i></b> I cannot see how your views can be squared with what was actually written in the 1st Edition core book (page 180, emphases mine): &quot;<i><b>The Princes do not brook interference into what they consider to be their historical rights and privileges,</b> nor do <b>the Ancients</b> desire a powerful group which could thwart their aims. Therefore, <b>the Camarilla remains a weak and divided Sect of only moderate influence.</b></i>&quot; When was the last time any of the books stated that the Princes and <i>the Ancients</i> were antagonistic to the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to think that the conflation of the Princes with the Camarilla, and the resulting redefinition of the Camarilla, has been one of the most pernicious influences on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> It's been going on for a long time, I'll give you that, but at least as far as my interest in the setting is concerned, it's been more destructive than, say, making the Sabbat playable and giving them a quasi-heroic spin ever was. I have next to no interest in a simplistic Anarchs vs. Camarilla conflict when the very first book published for the game already managed to present a more complex and interesting setup than that. The struggle between the younger generations and the elders drives everything in the setting <i>regardless of sect and across all political boundaries.</i><br /> <br /> The original Camarilla could just as easily be a foil for the unchecked power of Princes as it could be a tool for the oppression of the anarchs. I have never read a single paragraph that has convinced me that I should be using the Revised or V5 redefinitions of the Camarilla instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:55:07-07:00","id":1460719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460717#post1460717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's been the case since Revised.<br /> <br /> The V5 version is not noticeably worse than the immediate previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The carmarilla has shifted into stupid evil rather than pragmatic evil. The anarchs have genrally become more toxic, criminal and awful, the god awful mommy ghouling springs to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-21-2021, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T13:08:21-07:00","id":1460724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460719#post1460719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The carmarilla has shifted into stupid evil rather than pragmatic evil. The anarchs have genrally become more toxic, criminal and awful, the god awful mommy ghouling springs to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Cleavers were in TIME OF THIN BLOOD.<br /> <br /> It's just Thin Bloods weren't Anarchs before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460718#post1460718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas I've never accepted the view that the Princes and the Camarilla are synonymous. <b><i>The office of the Prince is older than the Camarilla.</i></b> I cannot see how your views can be squared with what was actually written in the 1st Edition core book (page 180, emphases mine): &quot;<i><b>The Princes do not brook interference into what they consider to be their historical rights and privileges,</b> nor do <b>the Ancients</b> desire a powerful group which could thwart their aims. Therefore, <b>the Camarilla remains a weak and divided Sect of only moderate influence.</b></i>&quot; When was the last time any of the books stated that the Princes and <i>the Ancients</i> were antagonistic to the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to think that the conflation of the Princes with the Camarilla, and the resulting redefinition of the Camarilla, has been one of the most pernicious influences on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> It's been going on for a long time, I'll give you that, but at least as far as my interest in the setting is concerned, it's been more destructive than, say, making the Sabbat playable and giving them a quasi-heroic spin ever was. I have next to no interest in a simplistic Anarchs vs. Camarilla conflict when the very first book published for the game already managed to present a more complex and interesting setup than that. The struggle between the younger generations and the elders drives everything in the setting <i>regardless of sect and across all political boundaries.</i><br /> <br /> The original Camarilla could just as easily be a foil for the unchecked power of Princes as it could be a tool for the oppression of the anarchs. I have never read a single paragraph that has convinced me that I should be using the Revised or V5 redefinitions of the Camarilla instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with you but I also point out that the vast majority of Kindred are never going to meet a member of the Camarilla above the Prince level. If you ever meet a Justicar in a 1000 years, you're probably very unlucky as the majority of Kindred are only going to deal with the Camarilla through their local representatives. The office of Prince is far older than that of the Camarilla and pretty much exists as early as the time of Caine but the Camarilla more or less codefied the system and put themselves above them.<br /> <br /> You have people like Mithras who can ignore it but just about everyone else has to kiss the ring of the Inner Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T13:19:42-07:00","id":1460726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460715#post1460715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that were the case then vtm would be stillborn, all three of the sects are evil and full of awful awful people doing awful things. In fact they made the anarchs and cams worse than in previous editions. The chechya incident obviously being the worst offender because it broke the golden rule about irl politics but even the more....wholesome sections are pretty demented irl.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fear is precisely this, that VtM from now on will become a more &quot;family friendly&quot; version to avoid any kind of problem.<br /> <br /> I also think that neither Anarch and the Cam are anything more than terrible people, but I think someone with power within the WW thinks that the themes Sabbat touch are more &quot;dangerous&quot; to the game's image.<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt to remember that the backlashes happened after Core and the Anarch and Camarilla books were released, so it would be very difficult to change the things that were established in them.<br /> <br /> Since the Sabbat came later than that, they were able to &quot;fit&quot; it under the new editorial guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","name":"Mark Logan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T13:40:51-07:00","id":1460730,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> On the actual topic of the thread:<br /> <br /> I'm kinda frustrated that with 60 seconds, the guy couldn't have lingering on the write-up of one Path long enough for us to screen cap and transcribe it and see what the book is actually going to do with them in print.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's a decent looking book with VtM words in it, and my only real take away is continual vindication towards my negative criticisms of V5 core's layout decisions.<br /> <br /> On the issue of V5 not just being written for old players:<br /> <br /> V20 was the only VtM book ever written just for old players... and it still sold to new players... and revitalized the WoD for a whole new generation of gamers. VtM was a multimedia brand for most of the 90s and early 00s. VtM had prose (short, novella, stand alone novels, and multi-novel series), comic books, a CCG, boardgames and single deck card games, multiple video games, a TV show, and a WWE wrestler even licensed the name Gangrel for use as his schtick. VtM and the WoD spent most of the 90s as the biggest (though not that big) challenger to D&amp;D as people's first RPG.<br /> <br /> V5 doing things differently because it's meant to appeal to more people and more media presentations... needs to be unpacked and justified (or at least acknowledged not inherently a smart move on Paradox's behalf) because the original run of VtM was already good at that. Just repeating that V5 is meant to be the foundations of a bigger multimedia enterprise isn't enough. What are the changes actually doing that matter to that regard when the original managed it?<br /> <br /> On the issue of the Sabbat not being playable for V5 because of cultural reactions:<br /> <br /> If Paradox was worried about that, they'd scrap the RPG books completely and just go back to letting Onyx Path do whatever with them like they do with Exalted and the CofD. The introduction section of V5 is not shy about VtM being a game about horrible evil people. You can't make V5 family friendly by toning down the Sabbat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T13:42:33-07:00","id":1460731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460724#post1460724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The office of Prince is far older than that of the Camarilla and pretty much exists as early as the time of Caine but the Camarilla more or less codefied the system and put themselves above them.<br /> <br /> You have people like Mithras who can ignore it but just about everyone else has to kiss the ring of the Inner Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not sound like <i>&quot;a weak and divided sect of only moderate influence.&quot;</i> That's the thing I'm contesting: The decision to enshrine the Camarilla as some sort of vampire world government, which has been the direction of the game from at least the Revised era onward. The 1st/2nd Edition Camarilla was <i>explicitly</i> not that: &quot;[The Camarilla's] rule is far from absolute, and it serves as a debating-chamber more than a government.&quot; (1st Edition core, page 194).<br /> <br /> A <b><i>debating-chamber.</i></b> That's the first and last time you'll ever read the Camarilla described in those terms. Why should I put a fascist vampire world government with jack-booted thugs into the game when the original setting was so much more interesting and flexible in the types of stories that it allowed the GM and players to tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:03:22-07:00","id":1460734,"title":"","content":"Theres this common belief that &quot;Sabbat was a later edition to vtm&quot; . I want to point out...VTM came out in 1991 and Players guide to the Sabbat came out in 1992. Its been a PC playable part of the game for a very very very long time. And the idea that Sabbat was bad guy npcs for a long time, is just not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:09:02-07:00","id":1460735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460731#post1460731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does not sound like <i>&quot;a weak and divided sect of only moderate influence.&quot;</i> That's the thing I'm contesting: The decision to enshrine the Camarilla as some sort of vampire world government, which has been the direction of the game from at least the Revised era onward. The 1st/2nd Edition Camarilla was <i>explicitly</i> not that: &quot;[The Camarilla's] rule is far from absolute, and it serves as a debating-chamber more than a government.&quot; (1st Edition core, page 194).<br /> <br /> A <b><i>debating-chamber.</i></b> That's the first and last time you'll ever read the Camarilla described in those terms. Why should I put a fascist vampire world government with jack-booted thugs into the game when the original setting was so much more interesting and flexible in the types of stories that it allowed the GM and players to tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think you read the exact same thing completely different from me. The Camarilla I described is one that I put in terms of <i>never being encountered by the average vampire</i> beyond the local Prince, Sheriff, and Scourge. Think on that. That the Inner Council, Justicars, Archons, and other important &quot;world government&quot; of vampires is such an incredibly distant and outright IRRELEVENT part of your average Cainite's lives that the only people who do have to worry about them are the Princes themselves.<br /> <br /> I think that's canon.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the Camarilla is the local government to most vampires and heavily influenced by the Princes who are themselves only vaguely under control because the Camarilla doesn't bother controlling individual vampires' lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460734#post1460734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres this common belief that &quot;Sabbat was a later edition to vtm&quot; . I want to point out...VTM came out in 1991 and Players guide to the Sabbat came out in 1992. Its been a PC playable part of the game for a very very very long time. And the idea that Sabbat was bad guy npcs for a long time, is just not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are my 2nd favorite playable sect for a reason. You are 100% correct.<br /> <br /> Mind you, as the huge Sabbat fanboy that I am, I also recognize that the vast majority of players have always played Camarilla with Sabbat being a minority. Just like my boys, the Anarchs. Star Trek Online posted stats and it was something like 90% of players were Federation and 10% Klingon/Romulan. The Sabbat have almost always been playable but they are, to most players, antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:11:32-07:00","id":1460736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460731#post1460731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should I put a fascist vampire world government with jack-booted thugs into the game when the original setting was so much more interesting and flexible in the types of stories that it allowed the GM and players to tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well reqiuem has that base covered quite nicely and does it better, I'm coming to VTM for setting flavour. Plus The Camarilla even in its stupid evil V5 phase isnt a fascist regime. it's more of a federated Feudal obligarchy contrasted with the De jure Sabbat Theocratic Constitutional monarchy and the Anarch's Tribal Anarchies (if I'm feeling nice)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:13:17-07:00","id":1460737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460736#post1460736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well reqiuem has that base covered quite nicely and does it better, I'm coming to VTM for setting flavour. Plus The Camarilla even in its stupid evil V5 phase isnt a fascist regime. it's more of a federated Feudal obligarchy contrasted with the De jure Sabbat Theocratic Constitutional monarchy and the Anarch's failure to calcify a unified ideology,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>V5 Camarilla is actually the exact opposite of fascism in its traditional manner. The V5 Camarilla is WITHDRAWING from its previous desire to rule all Kindred.<br /> <br /> They're leaving any Kindred they don't think can cut the mustard to burn.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is notable that they now suspiciously resemble the Invictus and the Anarchs the Carthians with big Blood Cults playing a role now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:16:47-07:00","id":1460738,"title":"","content":"I dunno, i feel like for me any ways, V5 is very much return to our roots. Which is cool and all, but again for me, If I wanted that...i'd just take my first ed book off the shelf and run it lol. I want to give paradox/white wolf my money. I'm glad it attracted new players. But for me, there's nothing there for me to spend my money on. Which just makes me sad. But I am also just one person. If V5 makes bank for them? its a business and they should keep doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:38:05-07:00","id":1460743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460718#post1460718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm beginning to think that the conflation of the Princes with the Camarilla, and the resulting redefinition of the Camarilla, has been one of the most pernicious influences on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very sympathetic to that point. Many people conflate several things when speaking about the Camarilla. Sometimes it is perfectly fine to do so. At other times it leads people to trouble.<br /> <br /> The first thing is the Camarilla as the overall government of the undead. This is limited to only a few things. The Inner Circle, Justicars, Archons, and the system of Conclaves (which are explicitly called by Justicars). When Princes complain about the Camarilla, they are talking about this. It's the incipient super-government that is interfering with their ability to rule their domains. This is the &quot;debating chamber&quot; (perhaps referring to both the deliberations of the Inner Circle and the Conclaves).<br /> <br /> The second thing is to conflate it with the Princes ruling their domains. However, that is not an innovation or unique concept to the Camarilla as Elphilim says. It is almost hardwired into vampire society. Princes existed before the Camarilla. There are Princes who do not accept the authority of the Camarilla at all (like Siegfried in Vancouver). And Sabbat Cardinals/Archbishops are basically the same thing as a Prince just with another title. As are Anarch Barons (or any other title a vampire uses who rules in an anarch domain). But because Princes are the immediate and obvious authority figure, they get identified with the Camarilla. But the position by itself isn't Camarilla. Only if a Prince recognizes the authority of the Inner Circle in some degree is that Prince a member of the Camarilla. But that can be said about anyone.<br /> <br /> The last thing builds on the above. Anyone who acknowledges the authority of the Inner Circle is part of the Camarilla. But there is a huge difference between someone who is merely a citizen or resident (your average vampire) and the actual government (the Inner Circle and its servants). Your typical vampires aren't a kind of civil servants or the militia of the Camarilla. They're just vampires. And this is why &quot;Anarchs&quot; were still considered to be part of the Camarilla. If they were just struggles with the local Prince, the actual Camarilla didn't care. Those that weren't were considered to be actual criminals or fugitives. The Free States were a threat because they explicitly denied the Inner Circle, not most Anarchs who were usually just inexperienced or local dissidents unhappy with the Prince who hadn't yet learned the right way of playing the game.<br /> <br /> The issue is that for many people the game is about <i>sect conflicts</i>. Regardless of whether it is Camarilla versus Anarchs (or usually Princes versus Anarchs) or Camarilla versus Sabbat, they want the game to be about conflict between groups. Because most players are heavily oriented to combat, they gravitate to sect wars because sect wars gives that to them.<br /> <br /> However, the game does not need to be about sect wars at all. I know many people originally attracted to the game because they wanted to explore all the other cool stuff inherent in a pseudo-Anne Rice style vampire setting. Combat had its role in these games, but the games weren't heavily into the violence. They were about personal horror, or exploring mysteries, dark romance, and many other things. They weren't soldiers in an army.<br /> <br /> But the moment you turn everything into a sect war, then the ordinary vampires of the Camarilla have to get conscripted into an army and fight the other vampires in the minds of players. This is what leads them to conclusions like &quot;the Anarchs are just being used as cannon fodder for the Camarilla!&quot; or &quot;the Brujah and Gangrel must leave because they're only used as cannon fodder for the other clans!&quot; But neither of those conclusions actually make sense.<br /> <br /> If Anarchs fight the Sabbat, it's not because the Inner Circle of the Camarilla told them to do so. It's because they are fighting for their own domains against Sabbat intruders. And the Brujah and Gangrel aren't cannon fodder more than any other clan. This is an example of OOC thinking taking over. Because we, the players, see the in-clan Discipline sets of the Brujah and Gangrel as being better combat oriented, and players who like to fight therefore gravitate to those clans, we see them as being more martial than the others, and therefore the frontline fighters. But that doesn't make sense from an IC perspective. Going back to Chicago By Night, how many Brujah could really be said to be warriors? Gengis might. But Hank Cave? He's a beatnik poet. Dooley? He's actually a con artist who joined the Black Panthers merely to get some street cred that attracted a certain type of white liberal to give him money. Anita Wainwright? She's a student protester. Blackjack is a union organizer. None of these people are actual fighters. Many of them didn't even have a Discipline set on their character sheet that would make them so. Yeah, if in danger they can fight - but so would Alan Sovereign the Ventrue financier, Rosa Hernandez the animal rights activist, any of the band members of Baby Chorus, and others. Certainly the Wolfpack would be warriors. But that is because they are Archons. Being Gangrel is secondary to that. Lodin, on the other hand, despite being Ventrue has lots of combat Disciplines and originally lead his coterie into killing his enemies during the Great Chicago Fire. In most games that I've been in, it's often the player of a Nosferatu who plays the heavy of the PC group. In another group it was the Ventrue Pinkerton Detective who was the most capable combat character.<br /> <br /> After all, things like &quot;that costs more XP than this, so it is not ideal from a character building perspective&quot; is inherently an OOC perspective. People don't think like that in real life.<br /> <br /> So who would be good at combat and actually do the heavy lifting for the Camarilla in the sect wars has nothing to do with clans. It has to do with their character concepts. At best, certain clans have higher percentage of those types than others for a variety of reasons. But that's very different than saying &quot;Because we're in a sect war, everyone is conscripted and we're going to send those clans whose in-clan Disciplines make better fighters from a character creation perspective so you can make better use of that XP.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460718#post1460718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have never read a single paragraph that has convinced me that I should be using the Revised or V5 redefinitions of the Camarilla instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one reason among many that metaplot is a bad thing. It's one thing for one ST to take the game into the direction of constant sect wars. That can be fun. But it leaves the option for other STs to do other things. Metaplots though hijack the setting and divides fans because it essentially tells them, &quot;No, the way you want to run your game is wrong.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:48:18-07:00","id":1460744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460734#post1460734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres this common belief that &quot;Sabbat was a later edition to vtm&quot; . I want to point out...VTM came out in 1991 and Players guide to the Sabbat came out in 1992. Its been a PC playable part of the game for a very very very long time. And the idea that Sabbat was bad guy npcs for a long time, is just not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. They weren't included in the core rulebook, but I think the reason was 1) they were working the setting out as they want into published form and had to get cash coming in so they can pay the people who were writing the next thing, and 2) since they were introducing the setting, they knew they couldn't do everything in one instant dump, and therefore had to parcel it out in more digestible bits. So first they did the Camarilla clans. Then the Independent clans. And then they introduced the Sabbat clans when they were ready to detail that sect. The Lasombra and Tzimisce were already being mentioned in the first editions Player's Guide so thought was obviously being given to them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I never play Sabbat. But if you want something more like the vampires of old that enter a place, start eating people, and create new vampires, then that's the place to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:48:40-07:00","id":1460745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460704#post1460704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are terribly afraid to publish anything that might cause a negative reaction, as with the chapter on Chechnya, and that it will hinder the use of the IP in other medias.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that is an oranges and apples case. The Chechnya thing didn't caused a ruckus because it was Evil\u2122, it cause a ruckus because it offered a fictional explanation to a real situation. That is disrespect with people living with the actual horrors and complexities there. This is a problem that will arise every time you try to fictionalize something that is really going on, gore or no gore.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you're right that they may want to avoid some problems, and that it is a comprehensible fear. But not a valid one, exactly. It is common, but usually the result of such fears is either more backlash or disinterest than engagement. And a lot of media products all across the industry are actually avoiding &quot;problematic&quot; themes less than ever.<br /> <br /> \u200bGuide to the Sabbat isn't offensive. Gypsies is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460719#post1460719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the god awful mommy ghouling springs to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a good example of the current problem. It isn't that the Anarchs are ghouling children because they're evil. It's that the Anarchs are ghouling children because they're too dumb. They were literally discussing if it would be bad for the baby and ignoring the one person in the conversation warning against it. All because they wanted the kids to be silent, not for power or anything else.<br /> <br /> Evil done for stupid reasons and through stupid methods just isn't right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460726#post1460726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My fear is precisely this, that VtM from now on will become a more &quot;family friendly&quot; version to avoid any kind of problem.<br /> <br /> I also think that neither Anarch and the Cam are anything more than terrible people, but I think someone with power within the WW thinks that the themes Sabbat touch are more &quot;dangerous&quot; to the game's image.<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt to remember that the backlashes happened after Core and the Anarch and Camarilla books were released, so it would be very difficult to change the things that were established in them.<br /> <br /> Since the Sabbat came later than that, they were able to &quot;fit&quot; it under the new editorial guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think this is going to happen, I think it is worse than that.<br /> <br /> You see, the two first BIG scandals of V5 didn't happened after the Camarilla and Anarch books. They happened BEFORE THE CORE. It was the White-Supremacist outrage and the Pedo-Vamp from the pre-release. And opinions aside, WW not only maneuvered the situation reasonably well, they mostly stood their position. The Chechnya thing didn't happened until the Cam book. AFAIK the ghouling mommies didn't generated a lot of outside backlash, it generated backlash here, because it's awfully stupid. Evil, horrible, but in a particularly moronic way.<br /> <br /> No, there is a worse reason for everything befalling the Sabbat in V5: the lead author doesn't like 'em.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460730#post1460730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the issue of V5 not just being written for old players:<br /> <br /> V20 was the only VtM book ever written just for old players... and it still sold to new players... and revitalized the WoD for a whole new generation of gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 actually became the best introductory book for new players the game ever had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460735#post1460735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat have almost always been playable but they are, to most players, antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the antagonists have nothing to do with having rules for playing them. It is simply that most of the books are clearly written with this assumption. The fact that they have been playable for all that time just reinforces that making them unplayable makes zero sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460731#post1460731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should I put a fascist vampire world government with jack-booted thugs into the game when the original setting was so much more interesting and flexible in the types of stories that it allowed the GM and players to tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I don't like to put it in such terms, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> is right. If you like that feel and don't want to include the whole convoluted setting, Requiem covers you far better than any Masquerade edition will.<br /> <br /> This is basically the state of things. At some point 2nd edition had too much of a metaplot, and Revised definitely went too far. At some point the lore of the game was locked into that. I personally totally agree with you, and I discuss Masquerade more out of nostalgia than anything. For playing, I actually switched almost completely on Vampire to Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T14:53:24-07:00","id":1460747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, there is a worse reason for everything befalling the Sabbat in V5: the lead author doesn't like 'em. </div> </div> </div>See this is where I disagree. Justin Achilli was the developer and write for revised Sabbat. Which got the most detail, fleshing out and depth to them then at any other time. He is also the guy who wrote V5 Sabbat. I don't think he hates the Sabbat. I think he was given a design direction that forced Sabbat to be written this way in V5. That's my theory anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T15:00:55-07:00","id":1460748,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea that Achili doesn't like the Sabbat doesn't hold water. I could buy that all these decades later he regrets some of how he first handled the Sect and wasn't hard for Paradox to convince on their new vision, but it's pretty clear the vision come from higher up in the company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T15:48:19-07:00","id":1460754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460747#post1460747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See this is where I disagree. Justin Achilli was the developer and write for revised Sabbat. Which got the most detail, fleshing out and depth to them then at any other time. He is also the guy who wrote V5 Sabbat. I don't think he hates the Sabbat. I think he was given a design direction that forced Sabbat to be written this way in V5. That's my theory anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli is probably why this book exists.<br /> <br /> Jason Carl might have been against the Sabbat but it could have been from over his head.<br /> <br /> Achilli? Achilli loves the Sabbat in all their monstrous glory.<br /> <br /> He probably regrets not being there to help detail the Hecata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T16:40:21-07:00","id":1460759,"title":"","content":"I may have mixed name/roles up. Who's the guy who wrote the core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],