-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T16:57:23-07:00","id":1460761,"title":"","content":"<br /> In Heart of the Forest, a Werewolf video game, some information about the tribes is quite controversial, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris are treated as a tribe of supremacists who may have fallen to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> If the game's creators wrote the game with the information passed on by the authors of the future W5, we might have a pattern about the future of the entire WoD.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that a person or group within WW has a very specific view on the scenario and wants to somehow strip away everything that might, in their opinion, cause some controversy.<br /> <br /> I confess that if this is true, I am very uncomfortable with such a narrow view of the scenario, as it seems to me to have the potential to alienate many old players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","name":"Mark Logan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T17:10:30-07:00","id":1460763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460761#post1460761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Heart of the Forest, a Werewolf video game, some information about the tribes is quite controversial, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris are treated as a tribe of supremacists who may have fallen to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> If the game's creators wrote the game with the information passed on by the authors of the future W5, we might have a pattern about the future of the entire WoD.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that a person or group within WW has a very specific view on the scenario and wants to somehow strip away everything that might, in their opinion, cause some controversy.<br /> <br /> I confess that if this is true, I am very uncomfortable with such a narrow view of the scenario, as it seems to me to have the potential to alienate many old players.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can actually join the Get of Fenris in the game and call out the other tribes for slandering their name. It is just a ridiculously hard ending to get.<br /> <br /> That was a relief to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T18:26:32-07:00","id":1460773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460761#post1460761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Heart of the Forest, a Werewolf video game, some information about the tribes is quite controversial, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris are treated as a tribe of supremacists who may have fallen to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> If the game's creators wrote the game with the information passed on by the authors of the future W5, we might have a pattern about the future of the entire WoD.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that a person or group within WW has a very specific view on the scenario and wants to somehow strip away everything that might, in their opinion, cause some controversy.<br /> <br /> I confess that if this is true, I am very uncomfortable with such a narrow view of the scenario, as it seems to me to have the potential to alienate many old players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now if I held a gun to your head and told you to try and guess correctly which tribe the devs will definitely not made fall to the Wyrm in W5, which would you pick?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Even with the emergence (or more appropriately, prominence gain) of RADFEM in the last year. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And you are completely right. They very much let their personal opinion contaminate the material. Some have theorized somewhere that I don't remember now that Get of Fenris and Red Talons will be eliminated. In fact, I read somewhere that for $$ reasons only seven tribes will be released into the core, and the Garou nation will have been split into at least two factions.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> <br /> /RANT ON<br /> <br /> This way you eliminate Nazi and Fursonian Viking players in the new edition, right? As well as anyone who plays wrong.<br /> <br /> It's our fault. Werewolf has always been about being a poor human estranged from society, a human+, but a human nonetheless. No extravagant gifts and powers, you naughty brats! There is no personal horror of transforming into Crinos for more than one turn. Every edition after the first one was a horrible mistake yada yada.<br /> <br /> There will prob. be no apocalypse, and Fomori and spirits will be completely normal people wearing slightly stylish clothes and MAYBE a little make up, ala Supernatural (nothing against the series but come on...) and Tzimisce in V5. We will be taught how we were wrong all along and the whole game was aways just a subtext for people dealing with anger and stress management. We, the fanbase, are the culprits of doing the mistake of turning the game into X-Men of darkness. <br /> <br /> And the correction will comes at a good time. As converting to other media is a thing to have in mind from now on, and CGI is hella expensive, a bunch of people doing Gangster/Police subtext with mild allusions to mysticism. Tattoos, tooth collars, and bared teeth will show your character as a werewolf well enough. /s<br /> <br /> /RANT OFF<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T18:32:14-07:00","id":1460775,"title":"","content":"A reminder that, in fact, the game lets you join the Get of Fenris and reveals that instead of the local Get being Nazis they were actually a Polish resistance fighter group.<br /> <br /> The idea they are gone is thus very unlikely. Since, again, you can join them.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are also one of the tribes that team up with you in the game. So they're not gone either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T18:56:33-07:00","id":1460778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460761#post1460761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess that if this is true, I am very uncomfortable with such a narrow view of the scenario, as it seems to me to have the potential to alienate many old players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have erred on the person in question and won't call any particular name, but by the current pattern I do believe that's what's happening. Not a fear of controversy or a plan for multimedia, but simply someone with a narrow view of how the setting should be pushing things in this direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460773#post1460773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if I held a gun to your head and told you to try and guess correctly which tribe the devs will definitely not made fall to the Wyrm in W5, which would you pick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I want the Get gone, as I actually like Norse themes as much as most people, but... what would be the problem with that part?<br /> <br /> On the Red Talons, though, I'd say good riddance. Despite everything they could be as a concept, what they actually are is just simplistic, unrealistic and hateful. They either belong to the Wyrm or to a very deep overhaul of tribal culture, something I'm not feeling confident that W5 will achieve in any satisfactory way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:31:57-07:00","id":1460791,"title":"","content":"IMO werewolf works <i>because </i>the tribes have extremely strong and often offputting personalities, not in spite of it. I don't like the Child of Gaia or the Stargazers, the former must be hypocrites, the latter is just orientalism, yet they <i>work </i>because every tribe needs to be extreme because they're <i>tribes </i>that exhibit <i>tribalism </i>and they're all products of <i>Rage</i> and they represent an out-group of society so radicalism is their thing. While I don't want to go back to Black Furies sacrificing male babies, I'm against all forms of making tribes more moderate or accomading (Except perhaps the Wendigo, who are an unjustified racist caricature) <br /> <br /> But the thing is... vampires are the opposite of werewolves. They're not outgroups, they're the in-groups, they mix with the elites of society and rule over men. As an in-group, a moderate stance is what they need, so this wild and crazy V5 nuCam Vs Anarchs dynamic doesn't work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:37:12-07:00","id":1460792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460791#post1460791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is... vampires are the opposite of werewolves. They're not outgroups, they're the in-groups, they mix with the elites of society and rule over men. As an in-group, a moderate stance is what they need, so this wild and crazy V5 nuCam Vs Anarchs dynamic doesn't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It worked for Requiem.<br /> <br /> And you know, everywhere the Camarilla and Anarchs were actively at war.<br /> <br /> Which was numerous times in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:56:40-07:00","id":1460794,"title":"","content":"Requiem is a different kettle of the fish. There's a tacit understanding that the supernatural exist and the masquerade isn't a top priority. There's a lot more suspension of disbelief because, y'know, shadowy predators with huge disparity in power and limited resources are agreeing to use a multi-party system in their government? <br /> <br /> I for one, like it when worldbuilding is taken seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:59:02-07:00","id":1460795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460794#post1460794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem is a different kettle of the fish. There's a tacit understanding that the supernatural exist and the masquerade isn't a top priority. There's a lot more suspension of disbelief because, y'know, shadowy predators with huge disparity in power and limited resources are agreeing to use a multi-party system in their government?<br /> <br /> I for one, like it when worldbuilding is taken seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do take it very seriously. But I always felt the Anarchs were hurt badly by being considered part of the Camarilla. Now they actually feel like they can do something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T23:12:59-07:00","id":1460797,"title":"","content":"I really think that's just you failing to separate yourself from your characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T23:31:06-07:00","id":1460798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460797#post1460797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think that's just you failing to separate yourself from your characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, my primary characters for 20 years were two Sabbat Elders.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think the big difference between us is<b><u> not </u></b>that I see the Anarchs as heroes and you don't but that I see the Anarchs as every bit as scheming and corrupt as the Camarilla. Hence they're able to hold their own.<br /> <br /> In Cyberpunk 2077 terms, here's how I see Night City (By Night):<br /> <br /> Saburo Arasaka: Camarilla Prince<br /> Yorinobu Arasaka: Former Anarch turned Camarilla stooge<br /> Hanako Arasaka: Camarilla<br /> Goro: Sheriff of Night City<br /> Meredith Stout: Rival Camarilla faction head<br /> <br /> Rogue: Anarch Baron (secretly in league with the Camarilla)<br /> Dex: Anarch gang leader<br /> V: Anarch merc<br /> Jackie Welles: Anarch merc<br /> Johnny Silverhand: Anarch true believer<br /> <br /> They're all fighting for a piece of the pie versus &quot;freedom.&quot; The Anarchs are just dirtier and street veruss the Ivory Tower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T23:40:36-07:00","id":1460799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460794#post1460794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem is a different kettle of the fish. There's a tacit understanding that the supernatural exist and the masquerade isn't a top priority. There's a lot more suspension of disbelief because, y'know, shadowy predators with huge disparity in power and limited resources are agreeing to use a multi-party system in their government? <br /> <br /> I for one, like it when worldbuilding is taken seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find Requiem far more believable as a setting than Mascarade. The supernatural is still very much hidden and conflict between the Covenants rarely descend into all out war in the street.<br /> <br /> But the Covenants offer far more depth than the Camarilla, the Sabbat and the Anarchs because they can differ considerably in structure from place to place but still basically hold the same tenets true.<br /> <br /> All that unite the Circle is that they are pagans/neo-pagans Vampires. The Crone isn't even there in all their cults. They will bicker and oppose each other a lot. But if somebody comes in to threaten one of them, they'll band together to drive him off.<br /> <br /> The lack of Caine, Generations and the general idea that today's neonate is potentially the equal of today's elder also help deffuse the tension. There isn't as much hard wired difference between a Ventrue Embraced in 1015 and one Embraced in 2015. If the latter is crafty she'll survive long enough to become an elder and thus be respected by most of her peers. It's not really the case in Masquarade.<br /> <br /> But I won't deny Requiem is probably less popular that V:tM. Which is why I'd like a potential 3ed to ditch the Gangrel, Nosferatu and Ventrue name for something more unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T01:18:27-07:00","id":1460803,"title":"","content":"I personally think that having Camarilla and Sabbat as two equal sects that both control certain territories never made sense. I really like Sabbat as a shadowy organisation that do their attrocities, dark rituals and acts of sabotage towards the Camarilla in seacret.<br /> <br /> That said I really don't like V5 railroading the experience of playing VTM. The complete focus on personal horror through a very restrictive hunger and humanity system and the harsh punishment for failing to act in those boundries- together with a refusal to make intricate rules for anything else- make a lot of interesting campaigns either not possible or not enjoyable when staying true to the text. The decision to not making Sabbat a playable sect isn't surprising in that regard.<br /> <br /> And VTM isn't the only system that goes in this direction. 7th Sea is even worse in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 09-22-2021, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T01:30:54-07:00","id":1460804,"title":"","content":"It makes sense for the Sabbat to hold territories because sometimes they're going to, y'know, win. They were never depicted as equal sects, with Sabbat presence really only in the new world and a bit of Australia. VTM can't be like a TV show where the end of every episode has some bullshit that absolutely ensures the status quo remains the way it is. The Sabbat were an effective force and they are inherrently better organized than anarchs, yet V5 wants the two factions to swap places because... they like one more than the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T02:32:19-07:00","id":1460806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460778#post1460778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have erred on the person in question and won't call any particular name, but by the current pattern I do believe that's what's happening. Not a fear of controversy or a plan for multimedia, but simply someone with a narrow view of how the setting should be pushing things in this direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I said, it doesn't seem like something specific to V5, but to the whole WoD. It seems to me that a person or group is responsible for authorizing what may or may not be published, a kind of editorial board, and these people have a very particular vision about what would be acceptable or not.<br /> <br /> What has dismayed me about these new books is that in my view, and from what I can see reading this topic and others on this forum, it is also the opinion of other people, is that the view that the person in charge has about various things in WoD it does not match the reality of the scenario itself or is a distorted view of it.<br /> <br /> This issue of Get of Fenris, for example, from what I read in another topic, is a tribe that attracted groups of neo-Nazis who felt represented by the culture and ideas that the tribe represents.<br /> <br /> That's when the problem begins, since you've already read the scenario and tribebooks, especially those by Revised, more deeply, that Get of Fenris internally fights the defenders of this ideology and that they in no way endorse its values.<br /> <br /> The impression that remains is that the editor or curator believes, on a shallow reading, that the tribe really is abhorrent and must be removed or modified.<br /> <br /> In the video game I mentioned before and as CTPhipps said, it is possible to follow in the footsteps of your ancestors in a way, but the totem that introduces you on this path makes it clear that this is a new version of the tribe, even with another name, which in his view removes the &quot;problematic&quot; parts.<br /> <br /> As far as the Sabbat is concerned, I believe the WW has failed to accept or think of a way to make the sect an acceptable option for players. I sincerely wonder if this question of much of the Sabbat not following humanity is such an &quot;evil&quot; idea and unacceptable to publishers that the book only found the light of day through a work of internal persuasion by Justin Achilli.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","user":"Mark Logan","date":". 09-22-2021, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","name":"Mark Logan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T02:51:42-07:00","id":1460808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460804#post1460804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense for the Sabbat to hold territories because sometimes they're going to, y'know, win. They were never depicted as equal sects, with Sabbat presence really only in the new world and a bit of Australia. VTM can't be like a TV show where the end of every episode has some bullshit that absolutely ensures the status quo remains the way it is. The Sabbat were an effective force and they are inherrently better organized than anarchs, yet V5 wants the two factions to swap places because... they like one more than the other?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This interestingly emphasises the big issue with the Anarchs, their total lack of cohesion is inappropriate for their success. The truth is sabbat had institutions, governing bodies, philosophy and self policing. What's more these bodies were distinct from how the carmarilla operated. The anarchs don't really have anything along those lines which is why they don't work as a big boy group. Anarch guide could have solved that but failed and now the settings carrying water for poochie in vtm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-22-2021, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T03:13:08-07:00","id":1460809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460745#post1460745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I don't like to put it in such terms, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> is right. If you like that feel and don't want to include the whole convoluted setting, Requiem covers you far better than any Masquerade edition will.<br /> <br /> This is basically the state of things. At some point 2nd edition had too much of a metaplot, and Revised definitely went too far. At some point the lore of the game was locked into that. I personally totally agree with you, and I discuss Masquerade more out of nostalgia than anything. For playing, I actually switched almost completely on Vampire to Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feelings on <i>Requiem</i> are complicated, but I don't want to get into the weeds of it here. Long story short, the (early) setting of <i>Masquerade</i> is simply a better fit for my personal tastes, and it has nothing to do with nostalgia -- I didn't crack open a single World of Darkness book until the original game line had already come to an end in 2004.<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel like &quot;Just go play <i>Requiem!</i>&quot; is a <i>non sequitur</i> response to what I was talking about. I wasn't disagreeing with the basic concepts of the original setting, but only voicing my disagreement with the direction the game line has taken since 1st and early 2nd Edition, as was (accurately, in my view) detailed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> in post #37. I have little interest in <i>Vampire: The Sect Wars,</i> and I reject the idea that this is all that <i>Masquerade</i> has ever been good for.<br /> <br /> When Mark Rein-Hagen himself says that <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Of1JmwBlmNc&amp;t=2309s\" target=\"_blank\">metaplot is stupid</a>,</b> I feel like I'm justified in that position. This is not an appeal to authority -- you don't have to care about what Rein-Hagen thinks one way or the other. I'm simply pointing out that one of the chief creators of the franchise does not consider metaplot a strength of the game, so it's not far-fetched to suggest that <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> is more than just its metaplot (which really only became a thing in the Revised era, as far as I can tell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T03:50:07-07:00","id":1460810,"title":"","content":"Thus we obviously must go back to 1st edition. Like legitimately. <br /> <br /> A Beast I am Lest a Beast I become<br /> Morality is chosen, not Ordained. <br /> The Cam international. <br /> It consists primarily of Tremere, Toreador, Ventrue, Nosferatu, Brujah, Gangrel and Malkavian. <br /> Diablerie is a natural part of the vampire state<br /> The Inconnu are actually maybe a thing<br /> Becoming human again is possible! <br /> <s>Racism</s>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T06:01:08-07:00","id":1460820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460808#post1460808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This interestingly emphasises the big issue with the Anarchs, their total lack of cohesion is inappropriate for their success. The truth is sabbat had institutions, governing bodies, philosophy and self policing. What's more these bodies were distinct from how the carmarilla operated. The anarchs don't really have anything along those lines which is why they don't work as a big boy group. Anarch guide could have solved that but failed and now the settings carrying water for poochie in vtm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean literally the point of V5 is that they've gotten organized and that's why they're winning now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T07:08:39-07:00","id":1460828,"title":"","content":"Nah really the more I think about it the more I agree that METAPLOT IS DUMB. Like any metaplot. Good metaplot, bad metaplot. Wouldn't matter if Tremere got his perfect comeuppance or if the Anarchs unanimously became lilth worshippers and then used the power of friendship to strap the antideluvians on ICBMs heading for the sun. I don't mind the self-contained struggles of the vampire population in ST Petersburg because I can happily ignore it and nobody's going to tell me my game is wrong over an enjoyable read, but reads become significantly less enjoyable when suddenly they undermine the storyteller and players and new players come to your table expecting Y when you're playing a very incompatible X.<br /> <br /> From an OoC perspective, It's just shit. I don't give a fuck about Hardstardt or Rudi or other SNPCs. VTM works so well because it gives you a toolbox and so much room for making your own city. You have the groundwork for an ecosystem but freedom to make your own political model. Every metaplot development is, at absolute best, is another tool for the toolbox but more likely, at worst, you're going to have another kid dicking around in your sandpit, taking away your toys and smashing your finely made castles. The only good metaplot development in modern nights has been Ur-Shulgi waking up, because it provides more tools than it takes away and initially isn't so obtrusive (No Assamites came to your city, carry on, business as usual)<br /> <br /> From an in character perspective, it's just shit. We're playing with a slow-to-change immortal society that, before 1900, had a few upsets at the beginning of the early modern period, had the Tremere pop up a thousand years ago, and... otherwise mirrored mortal trends and didn't really make much noise. But now Vampires Twist and turn like a twisty turny thing and are lead by the stars of a soap opera. Yeah sure, &quot;Final nights&quot; and all that, but evangelicals have been claiming the end is nigh forever now and all they need to do is just keep pushing the date forwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460820#post1460820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean literally the point of V5 is that they've gotten organized and that's why they're winning now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explain: How are they now more organized.<br /> How are the Sabbat not organized<br /> and why any of this absolute bullshit would reasonably be happening if we assume half-rational actors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-22-2021, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T07:19:25-07:00","id":1460831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460820#post1460820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean literally the point of V5 is that they've gotten organized and that's why they're winning now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they didn't get organized the carmarilla just picked up its ball and went home and they dropped a bridge on the Sabbat so the Anarchs are 'winning in the same sense europe 'won' the Black death. Anarch book could have addressed this but didn't so were stuck with 3rd ed anarchs in a big boy stage which is a major issue moving forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-22-2021, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T07:22:36-07:00","id":1460834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460831#post1460831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but they didn't get organized the carmarilla just picked up its ball and went home and they dropped a bridge on the Sabbat. Anarch book could have addressed this but didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they did get organized in the sense that it says that the Ministry, Gangrel, and Brujah have formed a new organization and we have apparently professional Anarchs like Rudi working on taking cities like Berlin.<br /> <br /> But yes, THE ANARCHS provided almost no information on that versus vignettes on how mean they were to hikers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T07:34:36-07:00","id":1460836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460834#post1460834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they did get organized in the sense that it says that the Ministry, Gangrel, and Brujah have formed a new organization and we have apparently professional Anarchs like Rudi working on taking cities like Berlin.<br /> <br /> But yes, THE ANARCHS provided almost no information on that versus vignettes on how mean they were to hikers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just numbers, structurally they're still the same sect. Rudi's army is just a localized vigilante movement which I don't really see having a long term future for a number of realpolitik reasons if the plot armour comes off. ( masquerade breech risk, they're actually a danger to disenfranchised peoples rather than an asset etc)<br /> <br /> Although I'll conceed as a member of the lgbtq community I really really dislike rudi's army for simular reasons I dislike the gay coding of true blood so my judgement is deeply clouded on this. As a tangent rudis army would work better as a hunter group or a hollow one/orphan faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-25-2021, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T07:56:14-07:00","id":1460840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460836#post1460836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just numbers, structurally they're still the same sect. Rudi's army is just a localised vigilante movement which I don't really see having a long term future for a number of realpolitik reasons if the plot armour comes off. (Walking masquerade breech, they're actually a danger to disenfranchised peoples rather than an asset etc)<br /> <br /> Although I'll conceed as a member if the lgbtq community I really really dislike rudi's army for simular reasons I dislike the gay coding of true blood so my judgement is deeply clouded on this. As a tangent rudis army would work really well as a hunter group or a hollow one/orphan faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes and no because Rudi's army isn't exactly a vigilante army if it is part of the military of Berlin that has been taken from the Camarilla. It's just the army.<br /> <br /> 2. Certainly within your rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:10:53-07:00","id":1460841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460809#post1460809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel like &quot;Just go play <i>Requiem!</i>&quot; is a <i>non sequitur</i> response to what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why I don't like to put in those terms, but I couldn't help it.<br /> <br /> My point is, the metaplot dominates VtM now and have been for a long time. I like the first V20 books precisely because they're more agnostic on this and I didn't wanted BJD on principle. But it was inevitable.<br /> <br /> Today, and for a long time already, the metaplot is the main mark of VtM to go forward, and so it will be the way to go forward. You can stay playing your own thing with the 1st ed setting as basis and only adding whatever you like from other books, but the other books will just keep reminding you that you're playing your own thing and that they're not meant to support your setting.<br /> <br /> It isn't right. It is horrible. And now it is even worse, since they give support for even less styles of play. But it is what it is, we can't expect things to change now. Many buyers fully expect metaplot development. Most players want the books to delve into elements that take from that 1st ed feel. Masquerade won't go back.<br /> <br /> Now, I can't help with your feelings about Requiem, esp if I don't know them, but that was sincerely what worked for me. I found there many things I treasured in VtM in 1st edition and that were dumped to make room for the metaplot. And Requiem didn't dumped them, even when more elements are added they are easy to ignore or tweak to my needs without directly contradicting the setting. It was a genuine suggestion that worked for some people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460828#post1460828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah really the more I think about it the more I agree that METAPLOT IS DUMB. Like any metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, and in any setting, too. It doesn't work well in Legend of 5 Rings, it doesn't work well in Ravenloft, it doesn't work well in Warhammer 40K. The hell it would in any WoD game. Convoluted backstory is ok. Character story arcs, that work with a plot but in a smaller scope are ok. Making versions of the same setting in different time periods may work. But metaplot itself is stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:16:25-07:00","id":1460843,"title":"","content":"I admit, I didn't buy V20 books until BJD because I didn't see the point without metaplot. After all, I already had previous editions so if I wasn't a big rules junkie then why was I buying them if not for updates on the setting?<br /> <br /> I missed a lot of good books because of that attitude.<br /> <br /> Metaplot is basically what keeps a setting alive, though. It makes your world bigger and continuously moving forward. Not just centered on your PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:21:21-07:00","id":1460845,"title":"","content":"I've never minded metaplot simply because I treated as &quot;the news&quot; in gaming terms. The only Real prominent npc I've had show up was monconda heading up a siege and then the carmarilla players only knew off him rather than met him and having to deal with his raw political power. It actually worked quite well, like the emperors presence on the death star for the average Rebel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:27:53-07:00","id":1460847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460843#post1460843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaplot is basically what keeps a setting alive, though. It makes your world bigger and continuously moving forward. Not just centered on your PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of setting thrive without necessarily delving into metaplot, at least not that frequently. How many <i>By Night</i> books couldn't have been released without advancing world-spanning plots? Even a single character's plot may drive multiple books without an actual metaplot. Comes to mind Ravenloft's Van Richten's Guides and the Gazetteers, two lines that went a long way without need to advance any true metaplot (although there are caveats, but the metaplot wasn't what was driving the interest in the books).<br /> <br /> \u200bBut yeah, keeping interest in the setting and in the purchase of books is a challenge, and metaplot is an answer to that challenge. It is one of the many challenges faced by our hobby as a market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:41:39-07:00","id":1460850,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I do have the idea that the BEST metaplot is PC interactive.<br /> <br /> Transylvania Chronicles for example even if the metaplot was mostly already laid out.<br /> <br /> The Fall of London is how the majority of V5 changes SHOULD have been done.<br /> <br /> Make the PCs a major part of it potentialy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T09:28:40-07:00","id":1460855,"title":"","content":"That's a no brainer. The biggest sin of VtM's metaplot by far is that it almost never is something that happened in the hands of an unknown group or few people know the identity of the new Prince. There is no space for the PCs to be among the big names. Instead we have things like the shitty fall of Baba Yaga where the entire module is about your PCs watching the events unfold and witnessing Vasilisa killing the hag, without either helping or having the opportunity to even affect some side event. The most significant interaction possible is only significant for your players when anyone playing a Nosferatu is summarily killed for no other reason and no hope of escape other than refusing to go on the adventure to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T09:54:34-07:00","id":1460859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460841#post1460841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, the metaplot dominates VtM now and have been for a long time. I like the first V20 books precisely because they're more agnostic on this and I didn't wanted BJD on principle. But it was inevitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can tell you that literally the ONLY useful part of BJD for my games so far has been the V20 Dhampir and 16th Gen write ups, Blood Rot mechanics and the seed of an idea that powerwise the Antediluvians are just 4th Gens with more XP from one of the Sarcophagus options in \u201cThe Omega.\u201d That\u2019s basically two pages of crunch out of of 559 pages of useless metaplot about what\u2019s happened with (and how to center a campaign around the actions of) various SPC\u2019s not one player in all my years has ever given the slightest fart, much less an entire shit about.<br /> <br /> It was easily the most useless game product I\u2019ve ever acquired.<br /> <br /> V20\u2019s core book by contrast was amazingly useful in that it consolidated material that had been spread across dozens of long out of print supplements (ex. Rev core didn\u2019t include any Elder disciplines and had no bloodlines and, quick, without looking, which Revised book had the Baali and full Daimonion discipline descriptions in it?) all in a single well-organized and searchable PDF.<br /> <br /> I think one thing Phipps may not appreciate about V20 is how hard it was to get legal copies of the VtM game material prior to the V20 Renaissance if you didn\u2019t know someone who already owned the books. <br /> <br /> At one point I had to essentially rewrite and produce my own \u201cwhite book\u201d (a reference to my use of cheap white three-ring binders to hold printed copies of my rules document for players) for my Mage campaign just because trying to make characters when half a dozen people only have one core book between them is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t need new crap metaplot. I needed an available rulebook that players could actually go out and buy and I needed a copy for myself so we\u2019d all be playing from the same book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T10:04:20-07:00","id":1460861,"title":"","content":"The -most benefits least drawbacks- plot is thus:<br /> <br /> The Gangrel stay a main member of the Cam because of course they do. You can still play Anarch/Autuark gangrel this way <br /> Ur Shulgi wakes up and causes the schism, but the Cam aren't keen on wholesale adopting Assamites so the storyteller is free to do what they want with them on a city-by-city/game-by-game basis.<br /> The part where Ravnos wakes up? Didn't happen. Or it was chimistry, Or perhaps the Ravnos bounced back. I don't know enough about the rest of the week of nightmares to put forth an informed opinion. <br /> Augustus can get the chomp but the bloodlines of death should really diffuse into the mainstream sects rather than keep in their corner and forming something silly like the Hecata. Joining the rest of the vampires really provides the most options while having the least amount of bad impact. <br /> The Anarchs can develop more blood sorcery paths because that provided lots of interesting options and was really way less destructive than whatever the Tremere are doing in V5. <br /> Anything else from V5? Drop it. <br /> <br /> Most gains with least losses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T10:05:54-07:00","id":1460862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460859#post1460859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can tell you that literally the ONLY useful part of BJD for my games so far has been the V20 Dhampir and 16th Gen write ups, Blood Rot mechanics and the seed of an idea that powerwise the Antediluvians are just 4th Gens with more XP from one of the Sarcophagus options in \u201cThe Omega.\u201d That\u2019s basically two pages of crunch out of of 559 pages of useless metaplot about what\u2019s happened with (and how to center a campaign around the actions of) various SPC\u2019s not one player in all my years has ever given the slightest fart, much less an entire shit about.<br /> <br /> It was easily the most useless game product I\u2019ve ever acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, easily the best RPG product I have ever bought in 30 years of gaming.<br /> <br /> BJD is exactly what I want: plot, storytelling, and hooks.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'll never buy a product that has rules. I have rule books. What I want is storytelling help and adventures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T10:15:52-07:00","id":1460864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Logan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460806#post1460806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as I said, it doesn't seem like something specific to V5, but to the whole WoD. It seems to me that a person or group is responsible for authorizing what may or may not be published, a kind of editorial board, and these people have a very particular vision about what would be acceptable or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, that would be Paradox Interactive and their chosen staff to handle the WoD brand. Because that's how companies do things. Ever since the original WW merged with CCP, control over the content has ultimately been in the hands of people outside of the creative process. Every OPP made WoD book has had to be sent to someone else (first CCP, now Paradox) for approval; including content. If Paradox says no to something that OPP wants to do, it doesn't happen, because Paradox owns the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What has dismayed me about these new books is that in my view, and from what I can see reading this topic and others on this forum, it is also the opinion of other people, is that the view that the person in charge has about various things in WoD it does not match the reality of the scenario itself or is a distorted view of it. </div> </div> </div>More simply? There's a lot of people that disagree with the brand direction Paradox is taking the WoD, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This issue of Get of Fenris, for example, from what I read in another topic, is a tribe that attracted groups of neo-Nazis who felt represented by the culture and ideas that the tribe represents. </div> </div> </div>Because the Get of Fenris literally had a neo-Nazi faction within their ranks. For 1e and 2e, being part of them was not grounds for other Get to kill you on sight for being an evil shit. Neo-Nazi Fenrir were tolerated as radicals among the Tribe until Revised finally said, &quot;no, that's dumb, the Tribe doesn't tolerate them openly,&quot; and then in W20 they finally had the Get just off the Swords completely.<br /> <br /> It's not a shallow reading, and the editorial process lead to the Tribe being retconned to get rid of the idea that neo-Nazi Get are part of mainstream Get culture, and moving to the idea that the Get don't tolerate Nazi ideology in their ranks. The Get needed to be modified, or they were, on a deep reading, encouraging pro-Nazi sentiments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the Sabbat is concerned, I believe the WW has failed to accept or think of a way to make the sect an acceptable option for players. I sincerely wonder if this question of much of the Sabbat not following humanity is such an &quot;evil&quot; idea and unacceptable to publishers that the book only found the light of day through a work of internal persuasion by Justin Achilli. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat book was announced as an intended V5 product well before Justin was hired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460809#post1460809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Mark Rein-Hagen himself says that <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Of1JmwBlmNc&amp;t=2309s\" target=\"_blank\">metaplot is stupid</a>,</b> I feel like I'm justified in that position. This is not an appeal to authority -- you don't have to care about what Rein-Hagen thinks one way or the other. I'm simply pointing out that one of the chief creators of the franchise does not consider metaplot a strength of the game, so it's not far-fetched to suggest that <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> is more than just its metaplot (which really only became a thing in the Revised era, as far as I can tell).</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem (even though I agree with his assessment of metaplot as a tool for RPG books):<br /> <br /> Mark nearly bankrupted White Wolf, and his removal from his top position in the company coincided with the mid-2e explosion (not Revised) of both metaplot and sales that saved the company.<br /> <br /> White Wolf had a sizeable portion of customers that cared more about &quot;what happens next?&quot; to the metaplot than worrying about more useful gaming material, which added another revenue stream to make VtM and the WoD a major success during the supplement treadmill era.<br /> <br /> That's part of why the metaplot grew so much and by Revised was so prominent in the books (even to the point of starting to diminish its initial positives). That's why you can't really separate VtM and metaplot. We can wax on about how poorly metaplot was implemented (and if the value added was really worth it) but at the time of VtM becoming a brand that people recognized beyond some obscure little RPG, the &quot;living world&quot; the metaplot created was a huge part of the appeal to customers buying the books; even those of us that bought the damned metaplot focused supplements just to know what to exclude before new players came in with ideas from them.<br /> <br /> VtM is more than the metaplot. VtM's metaplot is stupid. But VtM's metaplot is also a significant portion of what made it what it is. It might not be a strength of the game, but it is a strength of the brand. It's extremely hard to escape the idea that most people who want to play VtM, want to do so while completely tossing the metaplot. The metaplot is essential to VtM's brand image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T10:28:17-07:00","id":1460867,"title":"","content":"Actually, the massacre of the Swords of Heimdall was done in Werewolf Revised not V20.<br /> <br /> Ethan Skemp said it was basically done because of the RL Neo-Nazi problem that Werewolf was suffering. White supremacist gamers would show up and claim to be &quot;just playing in-character.&quot;<br /> <br /> So they decided to make a dramatic show of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T11:06:46-07:00","id":1460873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460864#post1460864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Get of Fenris literally had a neo-Nazi faction within their ranks. For 1e and 2e, being part of them was not grounds for other Get to kill you on sight for being an evil shit. Neo-Nazi Fenrir were tolerated as radicals among the Tribe until Revised finally said, &quot;no, that's dumb, the Tribe doesn't tolerate them openly,&quot; and then in W20 they finally had the Get just off the Swords completely.<br /> <br /> It's not a shallow reading, and the editorial process lead to the Tribe being retconned to get rid of the idea that neo-Nazi Get are part of mainstream Get culture, and moving to the idea that the Get don't tolerate Nazi ideology in their ranks. The Get needed to be modified, or they were, on a deep reading, encouraging pro-Nazi sentiments.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I referred to shallow reading, I was pointing out precisely the fact that it seems to me that they might not be considering that this &quot;cleaning&quot; has already been done in past editions and that the tribe would still be marked by this issue.<br /> <br /> The truth is, I just wanted a clear statement of why this decision was made for the Sabbat to be just antagonists. What themes and concepts were considered problematic? Why couldn't they somehow be worked to become acceptable?<br /> <br /> I know that in today's world it would be too much to expect a clear statement, but it would be good to be more certain which way the V5 will go and the main one, why this path was chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13270-mark-logan","name":"Mark Logan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T11:22:32-07:00","id":1460877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460859#post1460859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20\u2019s core book by contrast was amazingly useful in that it consolidated material that had been spread across dozens of long out of print supplements (ex. Rev core didn\u2019t include any Elder disciplines and had no bloodlines and, quick, without looking, which Revised book had the Baali and full Daimonion discipline descriptions in it?) all in a single well-organized and searchable PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, I DO have almost all of the previous and yet welcomed the idea of having everything in one book for reference and rules updates, simple as they could be, and it delivered above my expectations, I'm a huge fan of the X20 corebooks since, even more than I'm already am of the X20 lines as a whole.<br /> <br /> And as I don't always play with the same group, V20 is the best entry for any new players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460864#post1460864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's how companies do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>And is not an inherently bad thing either. Every single entertainment franchise works that way, and company policy is what gives them cohesion, since they're not being written by the same artist every time. Companies can do it right or wrong, as individuals can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460864#post1460864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get needed to be modified, or they were, on a deep reading, encouraging pro-Nazi sentiments.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a complex can of worms, and ultimately I think offing the Swords was unavoidable.<br /> <br /> But I do think we must keep in mind that neo-nazis exist and we can't stop them from enjoying the game. So they'll be something we'll have to deal with from time to time regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460864#post1460864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metaplot is essential to VtM's brand image.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one big problem that many players underestimate greatly. It is too easy to call an artist a sellout, but actually no one can dedicate time and effort in the level we wish to create books, or any other form of art, without figuring a way to finance those projects.<br /> <br /> And the RPG market is small. As in ridiculously small. Far smaller even than its cultural impact or rate of interest. Developing sustainable profit strategies is by far its biggest challenge, and one that drives a lot of behind the scenes decisions all the time. Many people with genuine interest in making good games have to deal with this conundrum, and a lot of development happened in the last 20 years, but there is still a long way to go to make this a stable market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T11:54:47-07:00","id":1460880,"title":"","content":"A company can..and should sperate their metaplot from their rule books. I like the way D&amp;D 5e does it. Here's a book of just rules and mechanics. Here's a book on setting and canon., It boggles my mind why WOD can't simply do the same. the VTM corebook for v5 should have been metaplot agnostic with just some basics on the world and tools to build a game. If you want metaplot...making world books for those settings and stories for players to play in. You could have, Old World of Darkness, V20, and Paradox's Metaplot as three separate worlds with books to support them. That way people that love metaplot and those worlds can just buy those books. For those that want to play their own world they just need the core book and supplemental rule books they want. <br /> <br /> If I wanna play Ravenloft i buy the Ravenloft book, not I buy the core books to the game and thats it because its the only place for the metaplot. Just makes sense to me to do it that way. If it was structured that way..we wouldn't keep having to have these conversations of &quot;look what v5 did now with this thing I love from the stories&quot;. You could have sabbat be bad guys in the paradox setting, and playable in another using the same edition. I dunno why they didnt go that way, but thats what makes sense to me and seems to work pretty well for wizards of the coast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T12:17:16-07:00","id":1460883,"title":"","content":"The answer is brand identity.<br /> <br /> Simple and straightforward, linking rules to a specific universe was never a thing for D&amp;D, but was conversely THE thing with WoD (and many others).<br /> <br /> It is even more important if you keep in mind that, seriously, as many people as may be waiting for better rules for the game 'cause the rules always sucked, precisely because of that no one was after V5 just for the rules. Selling a book that is pure crunch is hard, and V20 already did it splendidly, so it would be a very hard sell.<br /> <br /> Would have to offer something simply astounding in terms of rules, an overhaul that was really, really, really big and really good. Something in the line with what they did, but of even greater scope, there must be more than crunch, but a reason to get that particular crunch.<br /> <br /> V20 did it by offering a veritable encyclopedia of rules that would replace the entirety of your Vampire library to a single book. D&amp;D offers really thorough changes in rules at every new edition. What would V5 offer? It is hard, given the brand identity, to offer something besides metaplot, even if this metaplot could be minimal.<br /> <br /> Heck, many fans were waiting specifically to see what happened to the setting after Gehenna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T12:28:03-07:00","id":1460884,"title":"","content":"must....not...talk shit about 5th ed.....Ravenloft......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T12:28:58-07:00","id":1460885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460862#post1460862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, easily the best RPG product I have ever bought in 30 years of gaming.<br /> <br /> BJD is exactly what I want: plot, storytelling, and hooks.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'll never buy a product that has rules. I have rule books. What I want is storytelling help and adventures.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, and I never need storytelling help because I always follow the same procedure; set up a sandbox where various NPCs have various motivations and goals (the two most key stats for my NPCs are \u201cHas X\u201d and \u201cWants Y\u201d). Then you turn your PC\u2019s loose and maybe plant an inciting incident and let the players do as they will.<br /> <br /> Because I consider any campaign where the most important things happening in the sessions are not whatever the PCs are doing to be dismal failures (this doesn\u2019t mean most important things in the world, but the most important things in the story of the PCs\u2026 ex. the final episode of the Clone Wars is Asohka and Rex attempting to escape Order 66 and a crashing star cruiser; its not as important as the rise of the Empire and all the stuff from RotS to the galaxy at large, but to the protagonists their choices and struggles and enemies were the most important parts of Rex and Asohka\u2019s story).<br /> <br /> It felt like every plot hook in BJD is the PCs get involved in whatever one of SPC\u2019s from the chapter is doing and how the PCs can become peripherally involved in this SPC\u2019s story. The PC\u2019s own hopes, dreams, goals and plans are irrelevant to these hooks.<br /> <br /> None of the SPC\u2019s presented is more interesting than a player\u2019s own PC or a storyteller\u2019s original NPCs they\u2019ve tailored to fit the PC\u2019s stories. None of the scenarios will be as relevant as the ones the PCs have organically inserted themselves into or even created through their own ambitions.<br /> <br /> And again, it\u2019s great that you have plenty of rules already. My point was that, until the V20 Renaissance, a lot of people, particularly ones who didn\u2019t even start until after 2002, didn\u2019t have those books and needed them. V20 (and M20) made my life and their lives easier because now everyone had their own copies of the rules and could read the supporting fluff at their own pace and didn\u2019t have to share the same book as they made up characters and had more than a few minutes to actually read the setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T12:35:13-07:00","id":1460888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460861#post1460861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The -most benefits least drawbacks- plot is thus:<br /> <br /> The Gangrel stay a main member of the Cam because of course they do. You can still play Anarch/Autuark gangrel this way<br /> Ur Shulgi wakes up and causes the schism, but the Cam aren't keen on wholesale adopting Assamites so the storyteller is free to do what they want with them on a city-by-city/game-by-game basis.<br /> The part where Ravnos wakes up? Didn't happen. Or it was chimistry, Or perhaps the Ravnos bounced back. I don't know enough about the rest of the week of nightmares to put forth an informed opinion.<br /> Augustus can get the chomp but the bloodlines of death should really diffuse into the mainstream sects rather than keep in their corner and forming something silly like the Hecata. Joining the rest of the vampires really provides the most options while having the least amount of bad impact.<br /> The Anarchs can develop more blood sorcery paths because that provided lots of interesting options and was really way less destructive than whatever the Tremere are doing in V5.<br /> Anything else from V5? Drop it.<br /> <br /> Most gains with least losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>A new edition wouldn't be needed for such changes: they are more like an errata or addendum to the V20 corebook :-D<br /> <br /> To give sense to a new edition, you need sweeping and interesting changes, while keeping enough of your past glory to reassure traditional customers. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, V5 wished to become another &quot;D&amp;D 5\u00b0 edition&quot; successt story, bringing together fans of traditional VtM, LARPers and fans of the Chronicles of Darkness: it unfortunately underestimated attachment to both V20 and Onyx Path as a brand (and no amount of licensing has significantly healed the rift).<br /> <br /> True, V20 has had much less physical distribution than V5, and also not that many books: V5 managed to bring back Vampire into bookstores and book-selling chains, so by itself this is good result.<br /> <br /> But unfortunately the V20/V5 rift won't heal: I hope they open up soon enough the Storytellers Vault to V5 projects, it would be useful to rally creativity around the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T12:44:07-07:00","id":1460889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460885#post1460885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> until the V20 Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>We should note that, in 7 years (2011-2018), V20 produced 12 books, the last one being a bridge towards V5: that's an average of less than two books a year, most of them available only as Print-on-Demand. Surely a Rebirth, and a crucial one for brand survival, but hardly a Renaissance.<br /> <br /> <br /> V5 came out in late 2018, and it already has 12 between books and adventures, with another one coming next month, the majority of them available through normal distribution. <br /> <br /> Considering the pandemic, that's quite a result.<br /> <br /> Also, as I've pointed out in another thread, international physycal distribution makes a difference: in 10 years we italians had 2 available V20 books, the corebook and the companion, with Lore of the Clans coming next month. With V5, we already have 5 available books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-22-2021, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T13:06:26-07:00","id":1460893,"title":"","content":"If we are using the same exact qualifiers for what constitutes a book for both v20 and v5. Those numbers are wrong. V20 would be at 15 and V5 would be 11 (currently, with Sabbat and Second Inquisition that brings that number to 13)<br /> <br /> V20: Vampire the Masquerade 20<sup>th</sup> anniversary ,Dust to Dust, V20 Companion, Children of the Revolution, Hunters Hunted 2, Anarchs Unbound, Rites of the Blood, Dread Name, Red List, Lore of the Clans, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra, Ghouls and Revenants, V20 Ready Made Characters ,V20 Starter Kit, Lore of the Bloodlines, Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary<br /> <br /> V5: Vampire the Masquerade 5<sup>th</sup> Edition, New Blood Starter Pack, VtM Quickstart, Camarilla Sourcebook, Anarch Sourcebook, Fall of London, Chicago by Night, Let the Streets Run Red, Vampire the Masquerade Companion, Cults of the Blood Gods, Children of the Blood<br /> <br /> I would also say v20 had far more in page count and content that's useable compared to what currently exists for V5. Also V20 was exclusively published by Onyx Path. V5 has had multiple partenrs and publishers. So..context is kinda important when comparing the two editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T13:13:27-07:00","id":1460894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460893#post1460893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are using the same exact qualifiers for what constitutes a book for both v20 and v5. Those numbers are wrong. V20 would be at 15 and V5 would be 11 (currently, with Sabbat and Second Inquisition that brings that number to 13)<br /> <br /> V20: Vampire the Masquerade 20<sup>th</sup> anniversary ,Dust to Dust, V20 Companion, Children of the Revolution, Hunters Hunted 2, Anarchs Unbound, Rites of the Blood, Dread Name, Red List, Lore of the Clans, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra, Ghouls and Revenants, V20 Ready Made Characters ,V20 Starter Kit, Lore of the Bloodlines, Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary<br /> <br /> V5: Vampire the Masquerade 5<sup>th</sup> Edition, New Blood Starter Pack, VtM Quickstart, Camarilla Sourcebook, Anarch Sourcebook, Fall of London, Chicago by Night, Let the Streets Run Red, Vampire the Masquerade Companion, Cults of the Blood Gods, Children of the Blood<br /> <br /> I would also say v20 had far more in page count and content that's useable compared to what currently exists for V5. Also V20 was exclusively published by Onyx Path. V5 has had multiple partenrs and publishers. So..context is kinda important when comparing the two editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected, I had not counted the reprint of Dust to Dust, pregens and Starter Kit, but the numbers are still towards V5 (we can also count the Book of Nod). <br /> <br /> The fact that V5 material is less usable is a matter of tastes: V5 material tried the Requiem way of in universe fiction for setting books. <br /> What was lauded in Requiem Clanbooks apparently did not work for V5 Sect books, at least for many customers. <br /> <br /> As for multiple publishers, so far this has mostly hurted V5! I did not expect Modiphius to fail so spectacularly, but in all their term as licensees, they managed to produce one campaign book and a pdf adventure, one third of what they had pitched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-22-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T13:24:11-07:00","id":1460897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460885#post1460885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, and I never need storytelling help because I always follow the same procedure; set up a sandbox where various NPCs have various motivations and goals (the two most key stats for my NPCs are \u201cHas X\u201d and \u201cWants Y\u201d). Then you turn your PC\u2019s loose and maybe plant an inciting incident and let the players do as they will.<br /> <br /> Because I consider any campaign where the most important things happening in the sessions are not whatever the PCs are doing to be dismal failures (this doesn\u2019t mean most important things in the world, but the most important things in the story of the PCs\u2026 ex. the final episode of the Clone Wars is Asohka and Rex attempting to escape Order 66 and a crashing star cruiser; its not as important as the rise of the Empire and all the stuff from RotS to the galaxy at large, but to the protagonists their choices and struggles and enemies were the most important parts of Rex and Asohka\u2019s story).<br /> <br /> It felt like every plot hook in BJD is the PCs get involved in whatever one of SPC\u2019s from the chapter is doing and how the PCs can become peripherally involved in this SPC\u2019s story. The PC\u2019s own hopes, dreams, goals and plans are irrelevant to these hooks.<br /> <br /> None of the SPC\u2019s presented is more interesting than a player\u2019s own PC or a storyteller\u2019s original NPCs they\u2019ve tailored to fit the PC\u2019s stories. None of the scenarios will be as relevant as the ones the PCs have organically inserted themselves into or even created through their own ambitions.<br /> <br /> And again, it\u2019s great that you have plenty of rules already. My point was that, until the V20 Renaissance, a lot of people, particularly ones who didn\u2019t even start until after 2002, didn\u2019t have those books and needed them. V20 (and M20) made my life and their lives easier because now everyone had their own copies of the rules and could read the supporting fluff at their own pace and didn\u2019t have to share the same book as they made up characters and had more than a few minutes to actually read the setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's important in my games is the roleplaying and that means that means that stuff about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> * New NPCs<br /> * New Adventures<br /> * New Events<br /> * New politics<br /> <br /> Is important. Basically, stuff to spark my imagination as a storyteller and give me ideas about how to do something and spice up the PCs unlife. Mind you, I *LOVE* NPCs and their stories. Even if I didn't buy a book like Chicago by Night for the material to use inside it, I would buy it for the stories to read inside them. NPCs are full of fascinating tales and lore that enrich the game.<br /> <br /> V20 is great and full of interesting stuff. OPP did an amazing job with it.<br /> <br /> But what I loved most from them?<br /> <br /> <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary<br /> Dread List, Red Names<br /> Children of the Revolution<br /> Anarchs Unbound </i>(which updated the Anarch metaplot)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what kind of supplements you would want. For me, the no. 1 any book should provide is adventure hooks and NPCs second with lord third.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460888#post1460888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But unfortunately the V20/V5 rift won't heal: I hope they open up soon enough the Storytellers Vault to V5 projects, it would be useful to rally creativity around the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think it exists outside of a handful of forums. V5 won Origins and is used on Twitch, Youtube, and plenty of other locations. Its important to some gamers but probably insignificant to the overall player base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-22-2021, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T14:31:49-07:00","id":1460906,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460884#post1460884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">must....not...talk shit about 5th ed.....Ravenloft......</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? Except by that cute boardgame from 4th edition there's no new Ravenloft book since 3.5...<br /> <br /> Joking, I really didn't read it yet to have an informed opinion, as much as I trust yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T16:02:36-07:00","id":1460910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460893#post1460893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are using the same exact qualifiers for what constitutes a book for both v20 and v5. Those numbers are wrong. V20 would be at 15 and V5 would be 11 (currently, with Sabbat and Second Inquisition that brings that number to 13)<br /> <br /> V20: Vampire the Masquerade 20<sup>th</sup> anniversary ,Dust to Dust, V20 Companion, Children of the Revolution, Hunters Hunted 2, Anarchs Unbound, Rites of the Blood, Dread Name, Red List, Lore of the Clans, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra, Ghouls and Revenants, V20 Ready Made Characters ,V20 Starter Kit, Lore of the Bloodlines, Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary<br /> <br /> V5: Vampire the Masquerade 5<sup>th</sup> Edition, New Blood Starter Pack, VtM Quickstart, Camarilla Sourcebook, Anarch Sourcebook, Fall of London, Chicago by Night, Let the Streets Run Red, Vampire the Masquerade Companion, Cults of the Blood Gods, Children of the Blood<br /> <br /> I would also say v20 had far more in page count and content that's useable compared to what currently exists for V5. Also V20 was exclusively published by Onyx Path. V5 has had multiple partenrs and publishers. So..context is kinda important when comparing the two editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another factor in those numbers; in the same span Onyx Path also released DAV20, Werewolf20 and all its supplements, Mage20 and it\u2019s supplements, Wraith20 and Changeling20\u2026 all of which are at least marginally compatible with V20.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re still waiting on W5 and, at the rate we\u2019re going, 2025 for M5 looks deliriously optimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T22:07:16-07:00","id":1460983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460897#post1460897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't think it exists outside of a handful of forums. V5 won Origins and is used on Twitch, Youtube, and plenty of other locations. Its important to some gamers but probably insignificant to the overall player base.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about musical theory, I can't articulate a long essay on why I prefer X song to Y song, and I'm not particularly interested in doing that, I only vaguely have an idea of what a time signature is and that there's something called an octave, but I do know I like X song more than Y song. Just because I don't talk about it doesn't mean that I can't recognize a vastly better product. Music, like literature, has a lot of subjectivity to it, there's a lot of reasons why people can like or dislike the band <i>Tool</i>, There's no reason to like the tone-deaf mashups my spendthrift dorm mate made, or my sister's singing (not even ironically) V5 is much more like the rich kid with a synthesizer he barely knows how to use than the <i>Tool </i>of V20, and for some people that goes without saying. Nobody has tried to get my sister in on their band. <br /> <br /> <br /> Look if Metaplot really drives sales then fine, just don't do it in a way that shits on my game. Every metaplot change in V5 does exactly that, it shits on my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T23:45:12-07:00","id":1460987,"title":"","content":"The metaplot is certainly a very important part of VTM, but I don't think that this means that we can't have one or more core rule books and suplemant books that advance the meta plot. V5 feels like a mess when trying to navigate the books.<br /> <br /> The metaplot of VTM was never really good, if you went in depth analysing it. I think that a lot of plotpoints V5 introduces are actually quite smart and more in line how institutions of power work. The thing V5 botches though, is giving an explaination why those events happen. Brujah leaves the Camarilla for example is in my opinion a good plot point. But the way to this plot point over Theo Bell made no sense imo. The Pyramid falling and Tremere fracturing is also a good plot point, but the raid on Vienna again makes no sense from the informations we have. I also really like Sabbat imploding, because their ideologies are not sustainable for a society. But the way to get there was way too abrupt. Lasombra trying to get to the Camarilla and the Camarilla requiring them to slaughter their former peers? Sounds great, but there is no information that the Lasombra as a group are banding together to do that and requiring the members to do that individually is again strange. The clans of death uniting to not being swept aside by the other clans? Great. But again, there is no build up for that except an awkward get together.<br /> <br /> And this leads me to my next complaint: For the large amount of pages V5 has already, there are actually very little hard facts and the ones we got are usually very surface level. Even Cults of the Blood Gods, which is certainly a step in the right direction, seems to gloss over a lot of important stuff. I kind of expected a thourough analysis of the clans that united into the Hecata and their motivations and reservations to join the other clans. But after reading it once I don't think that I got anything close to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 09-23-2021, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T06:35:21-07:00","id":1461010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460906#post1460906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> What are you talking about? Except by that cute boardgame from 4th edition there's no new Ravenloft book since 3.5...<br /> <br /> Joking, I really didn't read it yet to have an informed opinion, as much as I trust yours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> it's trying to be less openly racist basically, the same thing 5e has being doing all round by moving to cultures being evil, not races as a whole being evil or inferior, which is as much as I know really, not that interested in any d20 systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T06:59:11-07:00","id":1461017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460894#post1460894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that V5 material is less usable is a matter of tastes: V5 material tried the Requiem way of in universe fiction for setting books.<br /> What was lauded in Requiem Clanbooks apparently did not work for V5 Sect books, at least for many customers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that V5 hasn't used the style of Requiem's clanbooks. Some of the clanbooks were more like first person novels with interspersed, stand alone, in universe fiction pieces, followed by appendices for the crunch. Even those that didn't read like that, such as the Ventrue clanbook, fitted into a story contained within all five books. <i>Camarilla</i> has a little bit of that, while <i>Anarch</i>, as I recall, is more like a collection of articles and interviews about Anarch ways, without a story or context about the compilation itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T12:09:33-07:00","id":1461063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461010#post1461010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's trying to be less openly racist basically, the same thing 5e has being doing all round by moving to cultures being evil, not races as a whole being evil or inferior, which is as much as I know really, not that interested in any d20 systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I always found the idea of every goblin or every orc being evil dumb as fuck and never used it. And in fact the Gnoll treatment in Volo's was one of the few instances where the fluff actually convinced me that a whole species could be evil and that be fun, due to how they're created by Yeenoghu there. So... not saying anything about Ravenloft, but that doesn't seems to really relate a lot to the rest of 5th edition, if that's what it is.<br /> <br /> Think I've heard something about this, indeed, they trying to be less racist by the dumb road that is changing the setting instead of acknowledging the past. Which is a shame given that racism is literally a thing within the setting to be properly worked with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T12:31:21-07:00","id":1461072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461063#post1461063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I always found the idea of every goblin or every orc being evil dumb as fuck and never used it. And in fact the Gnoll treatment in Volo's was one of the few instances where the fluff actually convinced me that a whole species could be evil and that be fun, due to how they're created by Yeenoghu there. So... not saying anything about Ravenloft, but that doesn't seems to really relate a lot to the rest of 5th edition, if that's what it is.<br /> <br /> Think I've heard something about this, indeed, they trying to be less racist by the dumb road that is changing the setting instead of acknowledging the past. Which is a shame given that racism is literally a thing within the setting to be properly worked with...</div> </div> </div> </div>They are giving official options on how to remove it as a theme, rather than retgoning it afaik, but again picking this up by osmosis, not via actually playing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T04:11:59-07:00","id":1461183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461010#post1461010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> it's trying to be less openly racist basically, the same thing 5e has being doing all round by moving to cultures being evil, not races as a whole being evil or inferior, which is as much as I know really, not that interested in any d20 systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I obviously don't object to the Retcon of the vistani since they're blatently irl Romani/Travelor. But I've never really had a problem with pure evil races/cultures in fantasy. Daleks,Nephandi, Phyrexians, ithilid, and Skaven are awesome.<br /> My objections to Ravenloft 5th arnt really anything to do with moving forward with the times and are more the gentrification and sterlization of the setting into a generic fantasy setting away from it's gothic horror roots . A world like Ravenloft needs to be ugly dark and misrable to work. I've already got forgetten realms and the stats for Tannarii if I want to run a horror in a cleaner high fantasy when I run Ravenloft I want ignorant peasents, bigoted jerks who'll burn you alive for a wart, sanity blasting evil and bleak bleak moors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-24-2021, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T14:15:15-07:00","id":1461269,"title":"","content":"Kind of that. Mind you, in a setting like Ravenloft saying that every single &lt;<i>insert race here</i>&gt; is evil is insensitive and I'm not against it being removed.<br /> <br /> But saying that <i>most people of Barovia</i> think this is true or wouldn't ever accept a woman as a scholar is... fitting for the setting. You're portraying prejudices instead of pretending they don't exist, and saying out loud people like those exist, but they're wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T06:14:51-07:00","id":1461324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1460897#post1460897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the no. 1 any book should provide is adventure hooks and NPCs second with lord third.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st- setting info<br /> 2nd- Rules<br /> 3rd- NPCs<br /> <br /> I'll skim the fluff for metaplot i might like, and basically ignore any plot hooks.<br /> <br /> I ran a heavy scripted adventure <i>once</i>, after having to write as much, if not more than the published material to fill in the gaps. It kinda ruined GMing for me, haven't wanted to run anything since.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T13:19:47-07:00","id":1461408,"title":"","content":"One serious question I have, since I have the books but didn't read it all yet:<br /> <br /> If the Gehenna War happens everywhere, <b>what the hell is the Beckoning about!?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T13:21:52-07:00","id":1461409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461408#post1461408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One serious question I have, since I have the books but didn't read it all yet:<br /> <br /> If the Gehenna War happens everywhere, <b>what the hell is the Beckoning about!?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it was officially stated the Antediluvians are everywhere so the Beckoning is summoning them to more places than just the Middle East.<br /> <br /> Which is about as direct an answer as we're ever going to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:27:17-07:00","id":1461443,"title":"","content":"So the Antes are everywhere but nothing special is happening anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:42:13-07:00","id":1461445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461443#post1461443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Antes are everywhere but nothing special is happening anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently a larger than normal bunch of ancients were in the Middle East (no kidding) and the Sabbat took their war to the Ashirra that they previously had not but the initial assumption of &quot;Beckoning=Middle East&quot; has turned out to be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:46:23-07:00","id":1461446,"title":"","content":"My indignation is with Gehenna happening and the ancients walking around, no one of them seems to be doing anything of note. And not even this fact seem to be noticeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:58:39-07:00","id":1461449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460589-sabbat-book-take-a-peek?p=1461446#post1461446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My indignation is with Gehenna happening and the ancients walking around, no one of them seems to be doing anything of note. And not even this fact seem to be noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>My tablecanon is that 1/3rd of all Ancients and Elders have vanished. Which gives a nice round number for how much 